PathwayData.put("data/grammar_vocabulary/units/L08U2.json",{"strand":"grammar_vocabulary","level":8,"cefr":"B2a","unit":2,"theme":"Global Challenges","essential_question":"How can people work together to solve the world's biggest problems?","lessons":[{"id":"GV-L08-U2-LS1","title":"It Is Estimated That…: The Impersonal Passive with Reporting Verbs","objectives":["Students will be able to report facts and opinions formally with It is said that… and X is believed to…","Students will be able to choose to do, to be doing or to have done after the passive reporting verb.","I can write \"It is estimated that two billion people lack safe water.\"","I can write \"Lake Chad is said to have shrunk by ninety percent.\""],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من نقل الحقائق والآراء بأسلوب رسمي بـ It is said that… وX is believed to…","سيتمكن الطلاب من اختيار to do أو to be doing أو to have done بعد فعل النقل المبني للمجهول.","أستطيع أن أكتب It is estimated that two billion people lack safe water.","أستطيع أن أكتب Lake Chad is said to have shrunk by ninety percent."],"vocabulary":[{"word":"crisis","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈkraɪsəs/","definition":"a time of great danger or difficulty","arabic":"أزمة","example":"The country faced an energy crisis.","image_id":"GV-L08-U2-LS1-W01","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L08-U2-LS1-W01"},{"word":"shortage","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈʃɔrtədʒ/","definition":"a situation in which there isn't enough of something","arabic":"نقص / شُحّ","example":"There is a shortage of clean water in many villages.","image_id":"GV-L08-U2-LS1-W02","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L08-U2-LS1-W02"},{"word":"emissions","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ɪˈmɪʃənz/","definition":"gases sent into the air, especially from cars and factories","arabic":"الانبعاثات","example":"Factories must reduce their carbon emissions.","image_id":"GV-L08-U2-LS1-W03","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L08-U2-LS1-W03"},{"word":"drought","pos":"noun","ipa":"/draʊt/","definition":"a long period with little or no rain","arabic":"جفاف","example":"The drought destroyed the farmers' crops.","image_id":"GV-L08-U2-LS1-W04","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L08-U2-LS1-W04"}],"explanation":{"text":"News reports and academic texts often use the impersonal passive to give information without saying who said it, or to sound careful and objective. Pattern 1: It + is/was + said / believed / thought / estimated / reported / expected / known + that + clause: It is estimated that two billion people lack safe water.\nPattern 2: Subject + is/was + said / believed / thought… + to-infinitive: Agriculture is believed to use seventy percent of fresh water. Use to + base verb for the same time, to be + -ing for an action in progress (Droughts are reported to be getting worse), and to have + past participle for an earlier action (Lake Chad is said to have shrunk).\nDon't mix the two patterns: (not: The lake is said that it shrank) → It is said that the lake shrank / The lake is said to have shrunk. The reporting verb can be in the past too: It was believed that the Earth was flat.\nIt is said / believed / estimated / reported + that + clause\nSubject + is said / believed + to do (same time)\n… + to be doing (in progress) • … + to have done (earlier)\nDon't mix: (not: X is said that…)","examples":["It is believed that the ancient city was built around 300 BCE.","The new dam is expected to provide water for a million people.","Coral reefs are reported to be dying in many oceans.","It is estimated that the Amazon produces a huge amount of the world's oxygen.","The fire is thought to have started by accident.","Desalination is known to use a lot of energy.","It was once believed that the oceans could absorb any amount of waste.","The volunteers are said to have planted 5,000 trees in one day."],"common_errors":["✗ The lake is said that it has shrunk. → ✓ It is said that the lake has shrunk. / The lake is said to have shrunk. (Don't mix the two patterns.)","✗ The drought is believed to start in 2020. → ✓ The drought is believed to have started in 2020. (Earlier action → to have + past participle.)","✗ It is estimating that prices will rise. → ✓ It is estimated that prices will rise. (Passive → is + past participle.)","✗ Droughts are reported to get worse now. → ✓ Droughts are reported to be getting worse. (In progress → to be + -ing.)"],"arabic":"المبني للمجهول غير الشخصي يُستخدم في الأخبار والكتابة الأكاديمية لنقل المعلومة دون ذكر قائلها.\nالنمط الأول: It is said / believed / estimated + that + جملة: It is estimated that two billion people lack safe water.\nالنمط الثاني: الفاعل + is said / believed + to + الفعل: Agriculture is believed to use 70% of fresh water.\nto do للزمن نفسه، وto be doing للحدث الجاري، وto have done للحدث الأسبق، ولا نخلط بين النمطين."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “It Is Estimated That…: The Impersonal Passive with Reporting Verbs”. Let’s learn impersonal passive: It is said / believed / estimated / reported / expected that + clause; subject + is said / believed + to-infinitive (to do / to be doing / to have done) together.","on_screen":"GV-L08-U2-LS1 | It Is Estimated That…: The Impersonal Passive with Reporting Verbs","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"Listen to the start of “The World's Water Challenge”: Water is often called the most precious resource on Earth, but it is not shared equally. It is estimated that more than two billion people do not have safe drinking water at home. In many regions, droughts are reported to be getting longer and more severe. Look at the green words.","on_screen":"Water is often called the most precious resource on Earth, but it is not shared equally. It is estimated that more than two billion people do not have safe drinking water at home. In many regions, droughts are reported to be getting longer and more severe.","visual":"Image GV-L08-U2-LS1-IMG01 animates gently; target words glow Leaf Green as they are spoken."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"News reports and academic texts often use the impersonal passive to give information without saying who said it, or to sound careful and objective. Pattern 1: It + is/was + said / believed / thought / estimated / reported / expected / known + that + clause: It is estimated that two billion people lack safe water. Pattern 2: Subject + is/was + said / believed / thought… + to-infinitive: Agriculture is believed to use seventy percent of fresh water. Use to + base verb for the same time, to be + -ing for an action in progress (Droughts are reported to be getting worse), and to have + past participle for an earlier action (Lake Chad is said to have shrunk).","on_screen":"It is said / believed / estimated / reported + that + clause • Subject + is said / believed + to do (same time) • … + to be doing (in progress) • … + to have done (earlier)","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. It is believed that the ancient city was built around 300 BCE. The new dam is expected to provide water for a million people. Coral reefs are reported to be dying in many oceans.","on_screen":"It is believed that the ancient city was built around 300 BCE. / The new dam is expected to provide water for a million people. / Coral reefs are reported to be dying in many oceans.","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “The lake is said that it has shrunk.” That’s not right. We say: “It is said that the lake has shrunk. / The lake is said to have shrunk.” Don't mix the two patterns.","on_screen":"✗ The lake is said that it has shrunk.   ✓ It is said that the lake has shrunk. / The lake is said to have shrunk.","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:05","narration":"Quick check: \"The lake is said to have shrunk.\" Did the shrinking happen before now? … Think! … Yes – *to have shrunk* = earlier. Great job! Now you can say: I can write \"It is estimated that two billion people lack safe water.\"","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can write \"It is estimated that two billion people lack safe water.\"","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: impersonal passive: It is said / believed / estimated / reported / expected that + clause; subject + is said / believed + to-infinitive (to do / to be doing / to have done).","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","المبني للمجهول غير الشخصي يُستخدم في الأخبار والكتابة الأكاديمية لنقل المعلومة دون ذكر قائلها.","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: The lake is said that it has shrunk. — الصحيح: It is said that the lake has shrunk. / The lake is said to have shrunk.","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أكتب It is estimated that two billion people lack safe water."]},"texts":[{"type":"reading","title":"The World's Water Challenge","body":"Water is often called the most precious resource on Earth, but it is not shared equally. It is estimated that more than two billion people do not have safe drinking water at home. In many regions, droughts are reported to be getting longer and more severe.\nAgriculture is believed to use about seventy percent of the world's fresh water. As the global population grows, demand for water is expected to rise significantly by 2050. It is feared that water shortages could lead to new conflicts between countries that share rivers.\nSome of the damage has already been done. Lake Chad in Africa, for example, is said to have shrunk by around ninety percent since the 1960s. Millions of people who depend on it for fishing and farming have been affected.\nHowever, there is hope. Saudi Arabia, where rain is rare, is known to be one of the world's largest producers of desalinated water—seawater with the salt removed. New solar-powered plants are thought to be cleaner than older ones. In addition, the Saudi Green Initiative plans to plant ten billion trees across the country, which is expected to reduce dust storms and protect the soil.\nIt is widely agreed that no single country can solve the water crisis alone. Experts say that cooperation, new technology and smarter habits at home will all be needed.","word_count":223,"audio_id":"AUD-GV-L08-U2-LS1-T1"}],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L08-U2-LS1-A1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Controlled practice: Choose the correct answer.","items":[{"q":"___ that more than two billion people lack safe drinking water.","options":["It is estimating","They are estimated","It estimates","It is estimated"],"answer":"It is estimated","explanation":"It + is + reporting verb (past participle) + that.","explanation_ar":"النمط It is said that."},{"q":"Agriculture is believed ___ about seventy percent of the world's fresh water.","options":["to use","that it uses","using","to have using"],"answer":"to use","explanation":"Subject + is + reporting verb + to-infinitive.","explanation_ar":"النمط Subject + is said to."},{"q":"Lake Chad is said ___ by about ninety percent since the 1960s.","options":["to have shrunk","to shrink","that it shrank","shrinking"],"answer":"to have shrunk","explanation":"Earlier action → to have + past participle.","explanation_ar":"الحدث الأسبق ← to have done."},{"q":"Droughts are reported ___ longer in many regions.","options":["that they get","getting to be","to be getting","to get yesterday"],"answer":"to be getting","explanation":"Action in progress → to be + -ing.","explanation_ar":"الحدث الجاري ← to be doing."},{"q":"","options":["The forest is thought that it is 500 years old.","It thinks that the forest is 500 years old.","It is thought that the forest is 500 years old.","It is thinking that the forest is 500 years old."],"answer":"It is thought that the forest is 500 years old.","explanation":"Don't mix the two patterns.","explanation_ar":"لا خلط بين النمطين."},{"q":"Water demand around the world ______ significantly by 2050, as populations grow and temperatures rise.\n\nWhich choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","options":["expects to be risen","is expected to rise","is expecting to rise","is expected rising"],"answer":"is expected to rise","explanation":"Subject + is + reporting verb + to-infinitive.","explanation_ar":"النمط Subject + is said to."}]},{"id":"GV-L08-U2-LS1-B1","type":"open","instructions":"Guided practice: Rewrite with the impersonal passive. Begin with \"It is…\".","items":[{"q":"People say that water is the most precious resource.  (It is said)","options":[],"answer":"It is said that water is the most precious resource.","explanation":"It + is + reporting verb (past participle) + that.","explanation_ar":"النمط It is said that."},{"q":"Scientists estimate that the glacier loses 30 meters a year.  (It is estimated)","options":[],"answer":"It is estimated that the glacier loses 30 meters a year.","explanation":"It + is + reporting verb (past participle) + that.","explanation_ar":"النمط It is said that."},{"q":"Experts expect that the new law will reduce pollution.  (It is expected)","options":[],"answer":"It is expected that the new law will reduce pollution.","explanation":"It + is + reporting verb (past participle) + that.","explanation_ar":"النمط It is said that."}]},{"id":"GV-L08-U2-LS1-B2","type":"open","instructions":"Guided practice: Rewrite with the subject + passive + to-infinitive.","items":[{"q":"People believe that the old well is 1,000 years old. (The old well…)  (subject + to-infinitive)","options":[],"answer":"The old well is believed to be 1,000 years old.","explanation":"Subject + is + reporting verb + to-infinitive.","explanation_ar":"النمط Subject + is said to."},{"q":"People think that the fire started near the road. (The fire…)  (to have + past participle)","options":[],"answer":"The fire is thought to have started near the road.","explanation":"Earlier action → to have + past participle.","explanation_ar":"الحدث الأسبق ← to have done."},{"q":"Reports say that sea levels are rising faster. (Sea levels…)  (to be + -ing)","options":[],"answer":"Sea levels are reported to be rising faster.","explanation":"Action in progress → to be + -ing.","explanation_ar":"الحدث الجاري ← to be doing."}]},{"id":"GV-L08-U2-LS1-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Report the world.","items":[{"q":"Write a sentence with \"It is believed that…\" about a global problem.","options":[],"answer":"It is believed that plastic pollution harms millions of sea animals every year.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses impersonal passive: It is said / believed / estimated / reported / expected that + clause; subject + is said / believed + to-infinitive (to do / to be doing / to have done) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write a sentence with \"is expected to…\" about the future.","options":[],"answer":"The new metro is expected to reduce traffic in Riyadh.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses impersonal passive: It is said / believed / estimated / reported / expected that + clause; subject + is said / believed + to-infinitive (to do / to be doing / to have done) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write a sentence with \"is said to have…\" about the past.","options":[],"answer":"The old palace is said to have had over a hundred rooms.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses impersonal passive: It is said / believed / estimated / reported / expected that + clause; subject + is said / believed + to-infinitive (to do / to be doing / to have done) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write a sentence with \"are reported to be…\" about something happening now.","options":[],"answer":"Many species are reported to be moving north because of rising temperatures.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses impersonal passive: It is said / believed / estimated / reported / expected that + clause; subject + is said / believed + to-infinitive (to do / to be doing / to have done) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write a sentence with \"It is not known…\".","options":[],"answer":"It is not known exactly how many species live in the deep ocean.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses impersonal passive: It is said / believed / estimated / reported / expected that + clause; subject + is said / believed + to-infinitive (to do / to be doing / to have done) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]},{"id":"GV-L08-U2-LS1-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: News report.","items":[{"q":"Write a headline about a global challenge.","options":[],"answer":"Rivers Drying Up Across the Region","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses impersonal passive: It is said / believed / estimated / reported / expected that + clause; subject + is said / believed + to-infinitive (to do / to be doing / to have done) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write 3 sentences of the report using three different impersonal passive forms.","options":[],"answer":"It is estimated that five rivers have dried up this year. The drought is thought to have started three years ago. Farmers are reported to be leaving their villages.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses impersonal passive: It is said / believed / estimated / reported / expected that + clause; subject + is said / believed + to-infinitive (to do / to be doing / to have done) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write one hopeful sentence with \"is expected to\".","options":[],"answer":"A new water project is expected to bring relief to thousands of families.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses impersonal passive: It is said / believed / estimated / reported / expected that + clause; subject + is said / believed + to-infinitive (to do / to be doing / to have done) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Ball Toss Sentences","mechanic":"spin_wheel","rules":["Students stand in a circle. The teacher says a cue word and throws the ball.","The catcher makes a sentence with the cue word and impersonal passive: It is said / believed / estimated / reported / expected that + clause; subject + is said / believed + to-infinitive (to do / to be doing / to have done).","If it is correct, the catcher chooses the next cue word and throws the ball to a new student.","If it is not correct, classmates help fix it, and the same student tries again."],"data":[{"label":"It is said that…"},{"label":"It is believed that…"},{"label":"It is estimated that…"},{"label":"is thought to…"},{"label":"is reported to be…"},{"label":"is said to have…"},{"label":"needs to be done"},{"label":"is expected to be…"}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"It ___ that the pyramids were built over about twenty years.","options":["is believed","has believed","believes","is believing"],"answer":"is believed","explanation":"It + is + reporting verb (past participle) + that.","explanation_ar":"النمط It is said that."},{"q":"The new solar farm is expected ___ electricity for 50,000 homes.","options":["to have provided yesterday","that provides","providing","to provide"],"answer":"to provide","explanation":"Subject + is + reporting verb + to-infinitive.","explanation_ar":"النمط Subject + is said to."},{"q":"The flood is thought ___ more than 300 houses last week.","options":["damaging","to damage","to have damaged","that damaged"],"answer":"to have damaged","explanation":"Earlier action → to have + past participle.","explanation_ar":"الحدث الأسبق ← to have done."},{"q":"Thousands of refugees are reported ___ the border at this moment.","options":["crossing to be","that they cross","to cross yesterday","to be crossing"],"answer":"to be crossing","explanation":"Action in progress → to be + -ing.","explanation_ar":"الحدث الجاري ← to be doing."},{"q":"","options":["It is said that the river was once full of fish.","It says that the river was once full of fish.","It is saying that the river was once full of fish.","The river is said that it was once full of fish."],"answer":"It is said that the river was once full of fish.","explanation":"Don't mix the two patterns.","explanation_ar":"لا خلط بين النمطين."},{"q":"","options":["The ancient city is known that it had a large library.","The ancient city is known to have had a large library.","The ancient city knows to have had a large library.","The ancient city is known to has had a large library."],"answer":"The ancient city is known to have had a large library.","explanation":"Earlier action → to have + past participle.","explanation_ar":"الحدث الأسبق ← to have done."},{"q":"___ that the oceans could absorb any amount of plastic.","options":["It once believed","It was once believed","They were once believed","It was once believing"],"answer":"It was once believed","explanation":"It + is + reporting verb (past participle) + that.","explanation_ar":"النمط It is said that."},{"q":"The Great Pacific Garbage Patch, a huge area of floating plastic in the ocean, ______ about 1.6 million square kilometers.\n\nWhich choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","options":["is estimated covering","is estimating to cover","is estimated to cover","estimates to cover"],"answer":"is estimated to cover","explanation":"Subject + is + reporting verb + to-infinitive.","explanation_ar":"النمط Subject + is said to."},{"q":"The fire that destroyed part of the forest last summer ______ by a broken glass bottle that focused the sun's rays.\n\nWhich choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","options":["is thinking to have started","is thought to start","is thought to have been started","thinks to have been started"],"answer":"is thought to have been started","explanation":"Earlier action → to have + past participle.","explanation_ar":"الحدث الأسبق ← to have done."},{"q":"Which sentence is the most formal?","options":["I heard the crisis is getting worse.","It is reported that the crisis is getting worse.","Everyone knows the crisis is bad.","People say the crisis is getting worse."],"answer":"It is reported that the crisis is getting worse.","explanation":"It + is + reporting verb (past participle) + that.","explanation_ar":"النمط It is said that."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L08-U2-LS1-IMG01","prompt":"A split world map: on one side, a dried-up lake bed with cracked earth and boats lying on sand; on the other side, a modern solar-powered desalination plant on the Red Sea coast and young trees being planted in the desert; infographic icons for water drops and percentages. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"A split world map: on one side, a dried-up lake bed with cracked earth and boats lying on sand; on the other side, a modern solar-powered desalination plant on the Red Sea coast and young trees being planted in the desert; infographic icons for water drops and percentages"},{"id":"GV-L08-U2-LS1-IMG02","prompt":"clean background panel for a grammar box about impersonal passive: It is said / believed / estimated / reported / expected that + clause; subject + is said / believed + to-infinitive (to do / to be doing / to have done), with Zaki the Falcon pointing at a blank board on the right; leave large empty space for text overlay. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"clean background panel for a grammar box about impersonal passive: It is said / believed / estimated / reported / expected that + clause"},{"id":"GV-L08-U2-LS1-W01","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows crisis (a time of great danger or difficulty); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing crisis: a time of great danger or difficulty"},{"id":"GV-L08-U2-LS1-W02","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows shortage (a situation in which there isn't enough of something); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing shortage: a situation in which there isn't enough of something"},{"id":"GV-L08-U2-LS1-W03","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows emissions (gases sent into the air, especially from cars and factories); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing emissions: gases sent into the air, especially from cars and factories"},{"id":"GV-L08-U2-LS1-W04","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows drought (a long period with little or no rain); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing drought: a long period with little or no rain"},{"id":"GV-L08-U2-LS1-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Ball Toss Sentences”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Ball Toss Sentences"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L08-U2-LS1-W01","script":"crisis. crisis. The country faced an energy crisis.","voice":"en-US, natural young-adult voice","speed":"1.0"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L08-U2-LS1-W02","script":"shortage. shortage. There is a shortage of clean water in many villages.","voice":"en-US, natural young-adult voice","speed":"1.0"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L08-U2-LS1-W03","script":"emissions. emissions. Factories must reduce their carbon emissions.","voice":"en-US, natural young-adult voice","speed":"1.0"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L08-U2-LS1-W04","script":"drought. drought. The drought destroyed the farmers' crops.","voice":"en-US, natural young-adult voice","speed":"1.0"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L08-U2-LS1-T1","script":"Water is often called the most precious resource on Earth, but it is not shared equally. It is estimated that more than two billion people do not have safe drinking water at home. In many regions, droughts are reported to be getting longer and more severe. Agriculture is believed to use about seventy percent of the world's fresh water. As the global population grows, demand for water is expected to rise significantly by 2050. It is feared that water shortages could lead to new conflicts between countries that share rivers. Some of the damage has already been done. Lake Chad in Africa, for example, is said to have shrunk by around ninety percent since the 1960s. Millions of people who depend on it for fishing and farming have been affected. However, there is hope. Saudi Arabia, where rain is rare, is known to be one of the world's largest producers of desalinated water—seawater with the salt removed. New solar-powered plants are thought to be cleaner than older ones. In addition, the Saudi Green Initiative plans to plant ten billion trees across the country, which is expected to reduce dust storms and protect the soil. It is widely agreed that no single country can solve the water crisis alone. Experts say that cooperation, new technology and smarter habits at home will all be needed.","voice":"en-US, natural young-adult voice","speed":"1.0"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L08-U2-LS1-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “It Is Estimated That…: The Impersonal Passive with Reporting Verbs”. Let’s learn impersonal passive: It is said / believed / estimated / reported / expected that + clause; subject + is said / believed + to-infinitive (to do / to be doing / to have done) together. Listen to the start of “The World's Water Challenge”: Water is often called the most precious resource on Earth, but it is not shared equally. It is estimated that more than two billion people do not have safe drinking water at home. In many regions, droughts are reported to be getting longer and more severe. Look at the green words. News reports and academic texts often use the impersonal passive to give information without saying who said it, or to sound careful and objective. Pattern 1: It + is/was + said / believed / thought / estimated / reported / expected / known + that + clause: It is estimated that two billion people lack safe water. Pattern 2: Subject + is/was + said / believed / thought… + to-infinitive: Agriculture is believed to use seventy percent of fresh water. Use to + base verb for the same time, to be + -ing for an action in progress (Droughts are reported to be getting worse), and to have + past participle for an earlier action (Lake Chad is said to have shrunk). Here are some examples. It is believed that the ancient city was built around 300 BCE. The new dam is expected to provide water for a million people. Coral reefs are reported to be dying in many oceans. Be careful! Some learners say: “The lake is said that it has shrunk.” That’s not right. We say: “It is said that the lake has shrunk. / The lake is said to have shrunk.” Don't mix the two patterns. Quick check: \"The lake is said to have shrunk.\" Did the shrinking happen before now? … Think! … Yes – *to have shrunk* = earlier. Great job! Now you can say: I can write \"It is estimated that two billion people lack safe water.\"","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"1.0"}]},{"id":"GV-L08-U2-LS2","title":"The Dam Is Expected to Be Finished Next Year: Passive Infinitives","objectives":["Students will be able to use to be done and to have been done after verbs and passive reporting verbs.","Students will be able to choose between active and passive infinitives.","I can write \"The rules need to be changed.\"","I can write \"The forest is thought to have been destroyed by fire.\""],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من استخدام to be done وto have been done بعد الأفعال وأفعال النقل المبنية للمجهول.","سيتمكن الطلاب من الاختيار بين المصدر المبني للمعلوم والمبني للمجهول.","أستطيع أن أكتب The rules need to be changed.","أستطيع أن أكتب The forest is thought to have been destroyed by fire."],"vocabulary":[{"word":"renewable","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/riˈnuəbəl/","definition":"coming from a source that does not run out, such as the sun or wind","arabic":"متجدّد","example":"Solar power is a renewable source of energy.","image_id":"GV-L08-U2-LS2-W01","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L08-U2-LS2-W01"},{"word":"conserve","pos":"verb","ipa":"/kənˈsɝv/","definition":"to use something carefully so it isn't wasted","arabic":"يحافظ على / يرشّد","example":"Turn off the tap to conserve water.","image_id":"GV-L08-U2-LS2-W02","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L08-U2-LS2-W02"},{"word":"poverty","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈpɑvɚti/","definition":"the state of being very poor","arabic":"الفقر","example":"Education helps families escape poverty.","image_id":"GV-L08-U2-LS2-W03","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L08-U2-LS2-W03"},{"word":"refugee","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈrɛfjudʒi/","definition":"a person who has to leave his country because of war or disaster","arabic":"لاجئ","example":"The camp gave shelter to thousands of refugees.","image_id":"GV-L08-U2-LS2-W04","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L08-U2-LS2-W04"}],"explanation":{"text":"A passive infinitive is to be + past participle. Use it when the subject receives the action: The dam is expected to be finished next year. (Someone will finish the dam.) The rules need to be changed. Every child deserves to be educated.\nThe perfect passive infinitive is to have been + past participle. Use it for an earlier action that was done to the subject: The forest is thought to have been destroyed by lightning. The paintings seem to have been damaged by water.\nCompare active and passive: The government expects to finish the dam. (The government finishes it.) ↔ The dam is expected to be finished. (The dam is finished by someone.) Common verbs: need, want, expect, hope, deserve, seem, appear, ask, plan + to be done.\nto be + past participle = passive (now / future)\nto have been + past participle = passive (earlier)\nneed / want / expect / hope / deserve / seem + to be done\nactive (to do) if the subject does the action; passive (to be done) if it receives it","examples":["The beaches need to be cleaned after every storm.","Endangered animals deserve to be protected.","The new law is expected to be passed next month.","The river appears to have been contaminated by a factory.","Refugee children want to be treated like any other children.","The vaccine is hoped to be ready by spring.","The ancient manuscripts are believed to have been hidden in a cave.","The committee asked for the report to be shortened."],"common_errors":["✗ The rules need to change by the committee. → ✓ The rules need to be changed by the committee. (The rules receive the action → passive.)","✗ The forest is thought to have destroyed by fire. → ✓ The forest is thought to have been destroyed by fire. (Passive → to have been + past participle.)","✗ Every child deserves to educate. → ✓ Every child deserves to be educated. (The child receives the action.)","✗ The dam is expected to be finish next year. → ✓ The dam is expected to be finished next year. (to be + past participle.)"],"arabic":"المصدر المبني للمجهول: to be + التصريف الثالث: The dam is expected to be finished next year.\nالمصدر التام المبني للمجهول: to have been + التصريف الثالث لحدث أسبق وقع على الفاعل: The forest is thought to have been destroyed by lightning.\nنستخدمه بعد need وwant وexpect وhope وdeserve وseem.\nإذا كان الفاعل يقوم بالفعل نستخدم المبني للمعلوم (to do)، وإذا وقع عليه الفعل نستخدم المبني للمجهول (to be done)."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “The Dam Is Expected to Be Finished Next Year: Passive Infinitives”. Let’s learn passive infinitives: to be + past participle (present/future) and to have been + past participle (past); after need, want, expect, hope, deserve, seem, appear and passive reporting verbs; active vs passive infinitive together.","on_screen":"GV-L08-U2-LS2 | The Dam Is Expected to Be Finished Next Year: Passive Infinitives","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"Remember these patterns: The trees need to be watered every day. The results aren't expected to be announced until June. When is the new hospital expected to be opened?","on_screen":"The trees need to be watered every day. | The results aren't expected to be announced until June. | When is the new hospital expected to be opened?","visual":"Pattern strips slide in from the left; the key words are highlighted in Leaf Green."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"A passive infinitive is to be + past participle. Use it when the subject receives the action: The dam is expected to be finished next year. (Someone will finish the dam.) The rules need to be changed. Every child deserves to be educated. The perfect passive infinitive is to have been + past participle. Use it for an earlier action that was done to the subject: The forest is thought to have been destroyed by lightning. The paintings seem to have been damaged by water.","on_screen":"to be + past participle = passive (now / future) • to have been + past participle = passive (earlier) • need / want / expect / hope / deserve / seem + to be done","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. The beaches need to be cleaned after every storm. Endangered animals deserve to be protected. The new law is expected to be passed next month.","on_screen":"The beaches need to be cleaned after every storm. / Endangered animals deserve to be protected. / The new law is expected to be passed next month.","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “The rules need to change by the committee.” That’s not right. We say: “The rules need to be changed by the committee.” The rules receive the action → passive.","on_screen":"✗ The rules need to change by the committee.   ✓ The rules need to be changed by the committee.","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:05","narration":"Quick check: \"The trees need to be watered.\" Do the trees water something? … Think! … No – someone waters them. Great job! Now you can say: I can write \"The rules need to be changed.\"","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can write \"The rules need to be changed.\"","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: passive infinitives: to be + past participle (present/future) and to have been + past participle (past); after need, want, expect, hope, deserve, seem, appear and passive reporting verbs; active vs passive infinitive.","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","المصدر المبني للمجهول: to be + التصريف الثالث: The dam is expected to be finished next year.","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: The rules need to change by the committee. — الصحيح: The rules need to be changed by the committee.","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أكتب The rules need to be changed."]},"texts":[],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L08-U2-LS2-A1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Controlled practice: Choose the correct answer.","items":[{"q":"The new dam is expected ___ next year.","options":["to have finished last","finishing","to finish","to be finished"],"answer":"to be finished","explanation":"to be + past participle (now/future).","explanation_ar":"to be done."},{"q":"The forest is thought ___ by lightning.","options":["to have destroyed","to have been destroyed","being destroyed","to destroy"],"answer":"to have been destroyed","explanation":"to have been + past participle (earlier).","explanation_ar":"to have been done."},{"q":"Endangered animals deserve ___.","options":["protecting","to have protect","to be protected","to protect"],"answer":"to be protected","explanation":"need / want / expect / deserve + passive infinitive.","explanation_ar":"الأفعال قبل المصدر المجهول."},{"q":"The government plans ___ ten new schools in the region.","options":["to build","to be built","to have been built","being built"],"answer":"to build","explanation":"Active or passive infinitive?","explanation_ar":"المعلوم أم المجهول؟"},{"q":"","options":["The river appears contaminating by the factory.","The river appears to be contaminate by the factory.","The river appears to have contaminated by the factory.","The river appears to have been contaminated by the factory."],"answer":"The river appears to have been contaminated by the factory.","explanation":"to have been + past participle (earlier).","explanation_ar":"to have been done."},{"q":"Many of the coral reefs near the coast ______ by rising sea temperatures over the past twenty years.\n\nWhich choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","options":["believe to have been damaged","are believed to have damaged","are believed to have been damaged","are believing to be damaged"],"answer":"are believed to have been damaged","explanation":"to have been + past participle (earlier).","explanation_ar":"to have been done."}]},{"id":"GV-L08-U2-LS2-B1","type":"gap_fill","instructions":"Guided practice: Complete with a passive infinitive. Word bank: to be replaced, to have been buried, to be announced","items":[{"q":"These old pipes need ______ (replace) before they leak.","options":[],"answer":"to be replaced","explanation":"need / want / expect / deserve + passive infinitive.","explanation_ar":"الأفعال قبل المصدر المجهول."},{"q":"The results are expected ______ (announce) on Thursday.","options":[],"answer":"to be announced","explanation":"to be + past participle (now/future).","explanation_ar":"to be done."},{"q":"The ancient coins are believed ______ (bury) by merchants.","options":[],"answer":"to have been buried","explanation":"to have been + past participle (earlier).","explanation_ar":"to have been done."}]},{"id":"GV-L08-U2-LS2-B2","type":"open","instructions":"Guided practice: Correct the mistake.","items":[{"q":"All plastic bottles need to recycle.","options":[],"answer":"All plastic bottles need to be recycled.","explanation":"to recycle → to be recycled. need / want / expect / deserve + passive infinitive.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: to recycle → to be recycled. الأفعال قبل المصدر المجهول."},{"q":"The paintings seem to have damaged by water.","options":[],"answer":"The paintings seem to have been damaged by water.","explanation":"to have damaged → to have been damaged. to have been + past participle (earlier).","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: to have damaged → to have been damaged. to have been done."},{"q":"The volunteers hope to be finished the work by sunset.","options":[],"answer":"The volunteers hope to finish the work by sunset.","explanation":"to be finished → to finish. Active or passive infinitive?","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: to be finished → to finish. المعلوم أم المجهول؟"}]},{"id":"GV-L08-U2-LS2-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Global needs.","items":[{"q":"Something in your city that needs to be fixed: ___","options":[],"answer":"The road near my school needs to be repaired.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses passive infinitives: to be + past participle (present/future) and to have been + past participle (past); after need, want, expect, hope, deserve, seem, appear and passive reporting verbs; active vs passive infinitive correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Something that deserves to be protected: ___","options":[],"answer":"The mangrove forests on the Red Sea coast deserve to be protected.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses passive infinitives: to be + past participle (present/future) and to have been + past participle (past); after need, want, expect, hope, deserve, seem, appear and passive reporting verbs; active vs passive infinitive correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"A project that is expected to be finished soon: ___","options":[],"answer":"The new sports stadium is expected to be finished next year.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses passive infinitives: to be + past participle (present/future) and to have been + past participle (past); after need, want, expect, hope, deserve, seem, appear and passive reporting verbs; active vs passive infinitive correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Something that seems to have been damaged: ___","options":[],"answer":"The old bridge seems to have been damaged by the floods.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses passive infinitives: to be + past participle (present/future) and to have been + past participle (past); after need, want, expect, hope, deserve, seem, appear and passive reporting verbs; active vs passive infinitive correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Something you want to be remembered for: ___","options":[],"answer":"I want to be remembered for helping others.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses passive infinitives: to be + past participle (present/future) and to have been + past participle (past); after need, want, expect, hope, deserve, seem, appear and passive reporting verbs; active vs passive infinitive correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]},{"id":"GV-L08-U2-LS2-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: Action plan.","items":[{"q":"Write 3 things that need to be done to save water in your school.","options":[],"answer":"Leaking taps need to be fixed. Plants need to be watered in the evening. Students need to be taught how to save water.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses passive infinitives: to be + past participle (present/future) and to have been + past participle (past); after need, want, expect, hope, deserve, seem, appear and passive reporting verbs; active vs passive infinitive correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write 2 sentences about an environmental problem using to have been + past participle.","options":[],"answer":"The beach seems to have been polluted by plastic. Many trees are thought to have been cut down illegally.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses passive infinitives: to be + past participle (present/future) and to have been + past participle (past); after need, want, expect, hope, deserve, seem, appear and passive reporting verbs; active vs passive infinitive correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write one sentence with \"deserve to be\".","options":[],"answer":"Farmers who protect the soil deserve to be rewarded.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses passive infinitives: to be + past participle (present/future) and to have been + past participle (past); after need, want, expect, hope, deserve, seem, appear and passive reporting verbs; active vs passive infinitive correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Dice Sentences","mechanic":"spin_wheel","rules":["Turn over a cue card and roll the die.","Make a sentence with the cue in the form shown by the die.","The player on the left checks; a correct sentence wins the card.","The player with the most cards after 7 minutes wins."],"data":[{"cue":"water / be / the most precious resource (It is said)"},{"cue":"droughts / get worse (are reported to be)"},{"cue":"the lake / shrink / since the 1960s (is said to have)"},{"cue":"the dam / finish / next year (is expected to be)"},{"cue":"the trees / plant / by volunteers (need to be)"},{"cue":"two billion people / lack / safe water (It is estimated)"},{"cue":"the fire / start / by lightning (is thought to have been)"},{"cue":"the new law / reduce / pollution (is expected to)"},{"cue":"the rules / change (should be)"}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"The streets need ___ after the sandstorm.","options":["to be cleaned","cleaning up to","to have cleaned","to clean"],"answer":"to be cleaned","explanation":"need / want / expect / deserve + passive infinitive.","explanation_ar":"الأفعال قبل المصدر المجهول."},{"q":"The winners are expected ___ at the ceremony tonight.","options":["to have announced last","to announce","to be announced","announcing"],"answer":"to be announced","explanation":"to be + past participle (now/future).","explanation_ar":"to be done."},{"q":"The documents are thought ___ in the fire.","options":["losing","to lose","to have lost","to have been lost"],"answer":"to have been lost","explanation":"to have been + past participle (earlier).","explanation_ar":"to have been done."},{"q":"Every refugee deserves ___ with respect.","options":["to be treated","treating","to treat","to have treat"],"answer":"to be treated","explanation":"need / want / expect / deserve + passive infinitive.","explanation_ar":"الأفعال قبل المصدر المجهول."},{"q":"The engineers expect ___ the bridge by May.","options":["being completed","to be completed","to have been completed","to complete"],"answer":"to complete","explanation":"Active or passive infinitive?","explanation_ar":"المعلوم أم المجهول؟"},{"q":"","options":["The well seems to be dig by hand.","The well seems to have been dug by hand.","The well seems to have dug by hand.","The well seems digging by hand."],"answer":"The well seems to have been dug by hand.","explanation":"to have been + past participle (earlier).","explanation_ar":"to have been done."},{"q":"","options":["The new hospital is hoped to be open by the ministry before winter.","The new hospital is hoped to be opened before winter.","The new hospital is hoped to open by the ministry before winter.","The new hospital is hoped opening before winter."],"answer":"The new hospital is hoped to be opened before winter.","explanation":"to be + past participle (now/future).","explanation_ar":"to be done."},{"q":"Who will build the dam in \"The dam is expected to be built by 2027\"?","options":["The dam builds itself.","Nobody knows if it exists.","Someone else – the dam receives the action.","It was built last year."],"answer":"Someone else – the dam receives the action.","explanation":"Who does the action?","explanation_ar":"مَن يقوم بالفعل؟"},{"q":"The ancient city of Hegra ______ by the Nabataeans more than two thousand years ago.\n\nWhich choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","options":["is known to have been built","is known to have built","knows to have been built","is knowing to be built"],"answer":"is known to have been built","explanation":"to have been + past participle (earlier).","explanation_ar":"to have been done."},{"q":"Before the new recycling plant opens, thousands of workers ______ to sort different types of plastic.\n\nWhich choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","options":["need training to be","need to train them","need to be trained","need to have trained"],"answer":"need to be trained","explanation":"need / want / expect / deserve + passive infinitive.","explanation_ar":"الأفعال قبل المصدر المجهول."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L08-U2-LS2-IMG01","prompt":"A construction site of a new dam in a green valley with a sign \"Expected to be completed 2027\"; a burned forest area with a sign \"Area to be replanted\"; volunteers carrying young trees. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"A construction site of a new dam in a green valley with a sign \"Expected to be completed 2027\"; a burned forest area with a sign \"Area to be replanted\"; volunteers carrying young trees"},{"id":"GV-L08-U2-LS2-IMG02","prompt":"two-panel visual contrasting correct and incorrect use of passive infinitives: to be + past participle (present/future) and to have been + past participle (past); after need, want, expect, hope, deserve, seem, appear and passive reporting verbs; active vs passive infinitive: a green tick panel and a soft red cross panel with simple objects from the theme “Global Challenges”; empty space for text overlay. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"two-panel visual contrasting correct and incorrect use of passive infinitives: to be + past participle (present/future) and to have been + past participle (past)"},{"id":"GV-L08-U2-LS2-W01","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows renewable (coming from a source that does not run out, such as the sun or wind); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing renewable: coming from a source that does not run out, such as the sun or wind"},{"id":"GV-L08-U2-LS2-W02","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows conserve (to use something carefully so it isn't wasted); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing conserve: to use something carefully so it isn't wasted"},{"id":"GV-L08-U2-LS2-W03","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows poverty (the state of being very poor); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing poverty: the state of being very poor"},{"id":"GV-L08-U2-LS2-W04","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows refugee (a person who has to leave his country because of war or disaster); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing refugee: a person who has to leave his country because of war or disaster"},{"id":"GV-L08-U2-LS2-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Dice Sentences”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Dice Sentences"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L08-U2-LS2-W01","script":"renewable. renewable. Solar power is a renewable source of energy.","voice":"en-US, natural young-adult voice","speed":"1.0"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L08-U2-LS2-W02","script":"conserve. conserve. Turn off the tap to conserve water.","voice":"en-US, natural young-adult voice","speed":"1.0"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L08-U2-LS2-W03","script":"poverty. poverty. Education helps families escape poverty.","voice":"en-US, natural young-adult voice","speed":"1.0"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L08-U2-LS2-W04","script":"refugee. refugee. The camp gave shelter to thousands of refugees.","voice":"en-US, natural young-adult voice","speed":"1.0"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L08-U2-LS2-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “The Dam Is Expected to Be Finished Next Year: Passive Infinitives”. Let’s learn passive infinitives: to be + past participle (present/future) and to have been + past participle (past); after need, want, expect, hope, deserve, seem, appear and passive reporting verbs; active vs passive infinitive together. Remember these patterns: The trees need to be watered every day. The results aren't expected to be announced until June. When is the new hospital expected to be opened? A passive infinitive is to be + past participle. Use it when the subject receives the action: The dam is expected to be finished next year. (Someone will finish the dam.) The rules need to be changed. Every child deserves to be educated. The perfect passive infinitive is to have been + past participle. Use it for an earlier action that was done to the subject: The forest is thought to have been destroyed by lightning. The paintings seem to have been damaged by water. Here are some examples. The beaches need to be cleaned after every storm. Endangered animals deserve to be protected. The new law is expected to be passed next month. Be careful! Some learners say: “The rules need to change by the committee.” That’s not right. We say: “The rules need to be changed by the committee.” The rules receive the action → passive. Quick check: \"The trees need to be watered.\" Do the trees water something? … Think! … No – someone waters them. Great job! Now you can say: I can write \"The rules need to be changed.\"","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"1.0"}]},{"id":"GV-L08-U2-LS3","title":"Tackle a Problem, Raise Awareness: Global-Issue Collocations","objectives":["Students will be able to use collocations to discuss global issues accurately.","Students will be able to choose precise words such as vulnerable, humanitarian and renewable in context.","I can say \"tackle a problem\", \"raise awareness\" and \"reduce emissions\".","I can describe global challenges with precise vocabulary."],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من استخدام المتلازمات لمناقشة القضايا العالمية بدقة.","سيتمكن الطلاب من اختيار كلمات دقيقة مثل vulnerable وhumanitarian وrenewable في السياق.","أستطيع أن أقول tackle a problem وraise awareness وreduce emissions.","أستطيع أن أصف التحديات العالمية بمفردات دقيقة."],"vocabulary":[{"word":"deforestation","pos":"noun","ipa":"/dɪˌfɔrɪˈsteɪʃən/","definition":"cutting down large areas of forest","arabic":"إزالة الغابات","example":"Deforestation destroys the homes of many animals.","image_id":"GV-L08-U2-LS3-W01","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L08-U2-LS3-W01"},{"word":"humanitarian","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/ˌhjuˌmænəˈtɛriən/","definition":"concerned with helping people who are suffering","arabic":"إنساني","example":"The organization sent humanitarian aid after the flood.","image_id":"GV-L08-U2-LS3-W02","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L08-U2-LS3-W02"},{"word":"vulnerable","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/ˈvʌlnɚəbəl/","definition":"easily hurt or harmed","arabic":"ضعيف / معرَّض للخطر","example":"Children and the elderly are the most vulnerable in a heat wave.","image_id":"GV-L08-U2-LS3-W03","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L08-U2-LS3-W03"},{"word":"inequality","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˌɪnɪˈkwɑləti/","definition":"an unfair situation in which some people have more opportunities than others","arabic":"عدم المساواة","example":"Inequality in education is a global problem.","image_id":"GV-L08-U2-LS3-W04","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L08-U2-LS3-W04"},{"word":"tackle","pos":"verb","ipa":"/ˈtækəl/","definition":"to make a serious effort to deal with a problem","arabic":"يعالج / يتصدّى لـ","example":"Governments must work together to tackle climate change.","image_id":"GV-L08-U2-LS3-W05","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L08-U2-LS3-W05"},{"word":"contaminate","pos":"verb","ipa":"/kənˈtæməˌneɪt/","definition":"to make water, food or air dirty or harmful","arabic":"يلوّث","example":"Chemicals from the factory contaminated the river.","image_id":"GV-L08-U2-LS3-W06","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L08-U2-LS3-W06"},{"word":"biodiversity","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˌbaɪoʊdaɪˈvɝsəti/","definition":"the variety of plants and animals in a place","arabic":"التنوع الحيوي","example":"Coral reefs are rich in biodiversity.","image_id":"GV-L08-U2-LS3-W07","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L08-U2-LS3-W07"}],"explanation":{"text":"Global issues have strong collocations: tackle / address / solve a problem; raise awareness of an issue; reduce / cut emissions; combat / fight climate change; provide / send humanitarian aid; pose a threat to; take action; conserve resources; protect biodiversity; face a crisis.\nUseful adjectives: renewable energy (from the sun, wind, water); vulnerable people (easily harmed); humanitarian aid (help for people who are suffering); a growing concern; severe drought; widespread poverty; endangered species.\nDon't translate word for word from Arabic: we raise awareness (not (not: make) awareness), take action (not (not: do) action), pose a threat (not (not: make) a threat), provide aid (not (not: give an aid) – aid is uncountable).\nCollocations/phrases: tackle a problem • address an issue • face a crisis • take action | raise awareness of • reduce emissions • combat climate change • conserve resources | provide humanitarian aid • pose a threat to • protect biodiversity • a growing concern | renewable energy • severe drought • widespread poverty • endangered species","examples":["Governments must take action now to combat climate change.","Our school campaign raised awareness of plastic pollution.","Plastic waste poses a threat to sea turtles.","The Red Crescent provided humanitarian aid after the earthquake.","Renewable energy can help countries reduce their emissions.","Older people are especially vulnerable during heat waves.","Deforestation is a growing concern in South America.","Education is one of the best ways to tackle poverty and inequality."],"common_errors":["✗ We made awareness about water waste. → ✓ We raised awareness of water waste. (raise awareness of.)","✗ The government did action. → ✓ The government took action. (take action.)","✗ They gave an aid to the refugees. → ✓ They provided aid to the refugees. (aid is uncountable.)","✗ Pollution makes a threat to fish. → ✓ Pollution poses a threat to fish. (pose a threat.)"],"arabic":"متلازمات القضايا العالمية: tackle a problem (يعالج مشكلة) وraise awareness (يرفع الوعي) وreduce emissions (يقلل الانبعاثات) وpose a threat (يشكّل تهديدًا).\nprovide humanitarian aid (يقدّم مساعدات إنسانية)، وaid اسم غير معدود فلا نقول an aid.\nلا نترجم حرفيًّا: نقول take action وليس do action، وraise awareness وليس make awareness.\nrenewable (متجدد) وvulnerable (معرّض للخطر) وbiodiversity (التنوع الحيوي)."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Tackle a Problem, Raise Awareness: Global-Issue Collocations”. Let’s learn collocations for global issues (tackle a problem, address an issue, raise awareness, reduce emissions, combat climate change, provide aid, pose a threat, take action, conserve resources); global-issue vocabulary together.","on_screen":"GV-L08-U2-LS3 | Tackle a Problem, Raise Awareness: Global-Issue Collocations","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"Meet some new words. deforestation: cutting down large areas of forest. humanitarian: concerned with helping people who are suffering. vulnerable: easily hurt or harmed.","on_screen":"deforestation | humanitarian | vulnerable","visual":"Each word card flips over to show its picture (vocabulary image briefs) and Arabic meaning."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"Global issues have strong collocations: tackle / address / solve a problem; raise awareness of an issue; reduce / cut emissions; combat / fight climate change; provide / send humanitarian aid; pose a threat to; take action; conserve resources; protect biodiversity; face a crisis. Useful adjectives: renewable energy (from the sun, wind, water); vulnerable people (easily harmed); humanitarian aid (help for people who are suffering); a growing concern; severe drought; widespread poverty; endangered species.","on_screen":"collocations for global issues (tackle a problem, address an issue, raise awareness, reduce emissions, combat climate change, provide aid, pose a threat, take action, conserve resources); global-issue vocabulary","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. Governments must take action now to combat climate change. Our school campaign raised awareness of plastic pollution. Plastic waste poses a threat to sea turtles.","on_screen":"Governments must take action now to combat climate change. / Our school campaign raised awareness of plastic pollution. / Plastic waste poses a threat to sea turtles.","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “We made awareness about water waste.” That’s not right. We say: “We raised awareness of water waste.” raise awareness of.","on_screen":"✗ We made awareness about water waste.   ✓ We raised awareness of water waste.","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:05","narration":"Quick check: Do we \"make\" or \"raise\" awareness? … Think! … *raise* awareness. Great job! Now you can say: I can say \"tackle a problem\", \"raise awareness\" and \"reduce emissions\".","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can say \"tackle a problem\", \"raise awareness\" and \"reduce emissions\".","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: collocations for global issues (tackle a problem, address an issue, raise awareness, reduce emissions, combat climate change, provide aid, pose a threat, take action, conserve resources); global-issue vocabulary.","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","متلازمات القضايا العالمية: tackle a problem (يعالج مشكلة) وraise awareness (يرفع الوعي) وreduce emissions (يقلل الانبعاثات) وpose a threat (يشكّل تهديدًا).","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: We made awareness about water waste. — الصحيح: We raised awareness of water waste.","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أقول tackle a problem وraise awareness وreduce emissions."]},"texts":[],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L08-U2-LS3-A1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Controlled practice: Choose the correct word.","items":[{"q":"Our school campaign ___ awareness of plastic pollution.","options":["raised","made","rose","did"],"answer":"raised","explanation":"Use the right collocation.","explanation_ar":"المتلازمة الصحيحة."},{"q":"Plastic waste ___ a serious threat to sea turtles.","options":["puts","poses","does","makes"],"answer":"poses","explanation":"Use the right collocation.","explanation_ar":"المتلازمة الصحيحة."},{"q":"The Red Crescent ___ humanitarian aid after the flood.","options":["rose","provided","made","did"],"answer":"provided","explanation":"Use the right collocation.","explanation_ar":"المتلازمة الصحيحة."},{"q":"Solar and wind power are ___ sources of energy.","options":["humanitarian","contaminated","vulnerable","renewable"],"answer":"renewable","explanation":"Choose the precise adjective.","explanation_ar":"الصفة الدقيقة."},{"q":"Cutting down large areas of forest is called ___.","options":["emissions","inequality","deforestation","biodiversity"],"answer":"deforestation","explanation":"Choose the global-issue word with the right meaning.","explanation_ar":"المعنى."},{"q":"Because they have little money and few resources, poor coastal communities are especially ______ to rising sea levels and storms.\n\nWhich choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","options":["renewable","indifferent","abundant","vulnerable"],"answer":"vulnerable","explanation":"Words in context (SAT style).","explanation_ar":"الكلمات في السياق."}]},{"id":"GV-L08-U2-LS3-B1","type":"match","instructions":"Guided practice: Match the verb to its partner.","items":[{"q":"tackle","options":["action before it's too late","carbon emissions from factories","an economic crisis","the biodiversity of coral reefs","water and electricity at home","a difficult social problem"],"answer":"a difficult social problem","explanation":"tackle → a difficult social problem. Use the right collocation.","explanation_ar":"المتلازمة الصحيحة."},{"q":"reduce","options":["action before it's too late","carbon emissions from factories","an economic crisis","the biodiversity of coral reefs","water and electricity at home","a difficult social problem"],"answer":"carbon emissions from factories","explanation":"reduce → carbon emissions from factories. Use the right collocation.","explanation_ar":"المتلازمة الصحيحة."},{"q":"conserve","options":["action before it's too late","carbon emissions from factories","an economic crisis","the biodiversity of coral reefs","water and electricity at home","a difficult social problem"],"answer":"water and electricity at home","explanation":"conserve → water and electricity at home. Use the right collocation.","explanation_ar":"المتلازمة الصحيحة."},{"q":"protect","options":["action before it's too late","carbon emissions from factories","an economic crisis","the biodiversity of coral reefs","water and electricity at home","a difficult social problem"],"answer":"the biodiversity of coral reefs","explanation":"protect → the biodiversity of coral reefs. Use the right collocation.","explanation_ar":"المتلازمة الصحيحة."},{"q":"face","options":["action before it's too late","carbon emissions from factories","an economic crisis","the biodiversity of coral reefs","water and electricity at home","a difficult social problem"],"answer":"an economic crisis","explanation":"face → an economic crisis. Use the right collocation.","explanation_ar":"المتلازمة الصحيحة."},{"q":"take","options":["action before it's too late","carbon emissions from factories","an economic crisis","the biodiversity of coral reefs","water and electricity at home","a difficult social problem"],"answer":"action before it's too late","explanation":"take → action before it's too late. Use the right collocation.","explanation_ar":"المتلازمة الصحيحة."}]},{"id":"GV-L08-U2-LS3-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Discuss global issues.","items":[{"q":"Which global issue worries you most, and why?","options":[],"answer":"Water shortage worries me most because our region is very dry.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses collocations for global issues (tackle a problem, address an issue, raise awareness, reduce emissions, combat climate change, provide aid, pose a threat, take action, conserve resources); global-issue vocabulary correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"How can students raise awareness of a problem?","options":[],"answer":"Students can raise awareness by making posters and short videos.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses collocations for global issues (tackle a problem, address an issue, raise awareness, reduce emissions, combat climate change, provide aid, pose a threat, take action, conserve resources); global-issue vocabulary correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Name one way to reduce emissions.","options":[],"answer":"People can reduce emissions by using public transportation.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses collocations for global issues (tackle a problem, address an issue, raise awareness, reduce emissions, combat climate change, provide aid, pose a threat, take action, conserve resources); global-issue vocabulary correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Who is most vulnerable during a crisis?","options":[],"answer":"Children and the elderly are most vulnerable during a crisis.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses collocations for global issues (tackle a problem, address an issue, raise awareness, reduce emissions, combat climate change, provide aid, pose a threat, take action, conserve resources); global-issue vocabulary correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write a sentence with \"humanitarian\".","options":[],"answer":"Saudi Arabia sends humanitarian aid to many countries.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses collocations for global issues (tackle a problem, address an issue, raise awareness, reduce emissions, combat climate change, provide aid, pose a threat, take action, conserve resources); global-issue vocabulary correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]},{"id":"GV-L08-U2-LS3-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: Model United Nations speech.","items":[{"q":"Choose a global issue and write an opening sentence with \"poses a threat to\".","options":[],"answer":"Plastic pollution poses a serious threat to marine life.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses collocations for global issues (tackle a problem, address an issue, raise awareness, reduce emissions, combat climate change, provide aid, pose a threat, take action, conserve resources); global-issue vocabulary correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write 2 sentences about what needs to happen, using 2 collocations.","options":[],"answer":"We must take action now. Every country should reduce its emissions.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses collocations for global issues (tackle a problem, address an issue, raise awareness, reduce emissions, combat climate change, provide aid, pose a threat, take action, conserve resources); global-issue vocabulary correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write one sentence with \"It is estimated that\" and one global-issue word.","options":[],"answer":"It is estimated that deforestation destroys millions of hectares of forest every year.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses collocations for global issues (tackle a problem, address an issue, raise awareness, reduce emissions, combat climate change, provide aid, pose a threat, take action, conserve resources); global-issue vocabulary correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Vocabulary Bingo","mechanic":"matching","rules":["Students write nine words from the list in their grid.","The teacher (or a student caller) reads a definition or Arabic meaning.","Students cross out the matching word.","Three in a row = \"Bingo!\" The winner must read the words and say what each means."],"data":[{"word":"crisis","match":"a time of great danger or difficulty","arabic":"أزمة"},{"word":"shortage","match":"a situation in which there isn't enough of something","arabic":"نقص / شُحّ"},{"word":"emissions","match":"gases sent into the air, especially from cars and factories","arabic":"الانبعاثات"},{"word":"drought","match":"a long period with little or no rain","arabic":"جفاف"},{"word":"renewable","match":"coming from a source that does not run out, such as the sun or wind","arabic":"متجدّد"},{"word":"conserve","match":"to use something carefully so it isn't wasted","arabic":"يحافظ على / يرشّد"},{"word":"poverty","match":"the state of being very poor","arabic":"الفقر"},{"word":"refugee","match":"a person who has to leave his country because of war or disaster","arabic":"لاجئ"},{"word":"deforestation","match":"cutting down large areas of forest","arabic":"إزالة الغابات"},{"word":"humanitarian","match":"concerned with helping people who are suffering","arabic":"إنساني"},{"word":"vulnerable","match":"easily hurt or harmed","arabic":"ضعيف / معرَّض للخطر"},{"word":"inequality","match":"an unfair situation in which some people have more opportunities than others","arabic":"عدم المساواة"},{"word":"tackle","match":"to make a serious effort to deal with a problem","arabic":"يعالج / يتصدّى لـ"},{"word":"contaminate","match":"to make water, food or air dirty or harmful","arabic":"يلوّث"},{"word":"biodiversity","match":"the variety of plants and animals in a place","arabic":"التنوع الحيوي"}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"All countries must work together to ___ climate change.","options":["rise","combat","make","do"],"answer":"combat","explanation":"Use the right collocation.","explanation_ar":"المتلازمة الصحيحة."},{"q":"The flood ___ a crisis for thousands of families.","options":["did","made up","rose","caused"],"answer":"caused","explanation":"Use the right collocation.","explanation_ar":"المتلازمة الصحيحة."},{"q":"Chemicals from the factory ___ the river.","options":["donated","conserved","tackled","contaminated"],"answer":"contaminated","explanation":"Choose the global-issue word with the right meaning.","explanation_ar":"المعنى."},{"q":"Many people had to leave their homes because of the war. They became ___.","options":["emissions","merchants","refugees","volunteers"],"answer":"refugees","explanation":"Choose the global-issue word with the right meaning.","explanation_ar":"المعنى."},{"q":"There's a ___ of doctors in rural areas.","options":["shortage","drought","crisis","poverty"],"answer":"shortage","explanation":"Choose the global-issue word with the right meaning.","explanation_ar":"المعنى."},{"q":"The rainforest is home to an amazing ___ of plants and animals.","options":["emission","biodiversity","inequality","deforestation"],"answer":"biodiversity","explanation":"Choose the global-issue word with the right meaning.","explanation_ar":"المعنى."},{"q":"Unfair pay between men and women is a form of ___.","options":["drought","inequality","biodiversity","shortage"],"answer":"inequality","explanation":"Choose the global-issue word with the right meaning.","explanation_ar":"المعنى."},{"q":"","options":["The charity did aid to the victims.","The charity provided an aid to the victims.","The charity provided food and medical aid to the victims.","The charity made aids to the victims."],"answer":"The charity provided food and medical aid to the victims.","explanation":"Use the right collocation.","explanation_ar":"المتلازمة الصحيحة."},{"q":"After three years without rain, the farmers faced a ______ drought that destroyed almost all of their crops.\n\nWhich choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","options":["severe","vulnerable","renewable","humanitarian"],"answer":"severe","explanation":"Words in context (SAT style).","explanation_ar":"الكلمات في السياق."},{"q":"The new campaign aims to ______ the problem of food waste by teaching families to plan their meals.\n\nWhich choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","options":["ignore","celebrate","contaminate","tackle"],"answer":"tackle","explanation":"Words in context (SAT style).","explanation_ar":"الكلمات في السياق."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L08-U2-LS3-IMG01","prompt":"A model United Nations classroom: students at desks with country flags, a screen showing icons for climate change, poverty, water shortage, deforestation and refugees; collocation cards on the board (\"tackle a problem\", \"raise awareness\", \"pose a threat\"). Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"A model United Nations classroom: students at desks with country flags, a screen showing icons for climate change, poverty, water shortage, deforestation and refugees; collocation cards on the board (\"tackle a problem\", \"raise awareness\", \"pose a threat\")"},{"id":"GV-L08-U2-LS3-IMG02","prompt":"word-web visual: a central circle with branches to 7 small picture icons of the lesson words; empty labels. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"word-web visual: a central circle with branches to 7 small picture icons of the lesson words"},{"id":"GV-L08-U2-LS3-W01","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows deforestation (cutting down large areas of forest); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing deforestation: cutting down large areas of forest"},{"id":"GV-L08-U2-LS3-W02","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows humanitarian (concerned with helping people who are suffering); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing humanitarian: concerned with helping people who are suffering"},{"id":"GV-L08-U2-LS3-W03","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows vulnerable (easily hurt or harmed); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing vulnerable: easily hurt or harmed"},{"id":"GV-L08-U2-LS3-W04","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows inequality (an unfair situation in which some people have more opportunities than others); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing inequality: an unfair situation in which some people have more opportunities than others"},{"id":"GV-L08-U2-LS3-W05","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows tackle (to make a serious effort to deal with a problem); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing tackle: to make a serious effort to deal with a problem"},{"id":"GV-L08-U2-LS3-W06","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows contaminate (to make water, food or air dirty or harmful); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing contaminate: to make water, food or air dirty or harmful"},{"id":"GV-L08-U2-LS3-W07","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows biodiversity (the variety of plants and animals in a place); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing biodiversity: the variety of plants and animals in a place"},{"id":"GV-L08-U2-LS3-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Vocabulary Bingo”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Vocabulary Bingo"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L08-U2-LS3-W01","script":"deforestation. deforestation. Deforestation destroys the homes of many animals.","voice":"en-US, natural young-adult voice","speed":"1.0"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L08-U2-LS3-W02","script":"humanitarian. humanitarian. The organization sent humanitarian aid after the flood.","voice":"en-US, natural young-adult voice","speed":"1.0"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L08-U2-LS3-W03","script":"vulnerable. vulnerable. Children and the elderly are the most vulnerable in a heat wave.","voice":"en-US, natural young-adult voice","speed":"1.0"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L08-U2-LS3-W04","script":"inequality. inequality. Inequality in education is a global problem.","voice":"en-US, natural young-adult voice","speed":"1.0"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L08-U2-LS3-W05","script":"tackle. tackle. Governments must work together to tackle climate change.","voice":"en-US, natural young-adult voice","speed":"1.0"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L08-U2-LS3-W06","script":"contaminate. contaminate. Chemicals from the factory contaminated the river.","voice":"en-US, natural young-adult voice","speed":"1.0"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L08-U2-LS3-W07","script":"biodiversity. biodiversity. Coral reefs are rich in biodiversity.","voice":"en-US, natural young-adult voice","speed":"1.0"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L08-U2-LS3-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Tackle a Problem, Raise Awareness: Global-Issue Collocations”. Let’s learn collocations for global issues (tackle a problem, address an issue, raise awareness, reduce emissions, combat climate change, provide aid, pose a threat, take action, conserve resources); global-issue vocabulary together. Meet some new words. deforestation: cutting down large areas of forest. humanitarian: concerned with helping people who are suffering. vulnerable: easily hurt or harmed. Global issues have strong collocations: tackle / address / solve a problem; raise awareness of an issue; reduce / cut emissions; combat / fight climate change; provide / send humanitarian aid; pose a threat to; take action; conserve resources; protect biodiversity; face a crisis. Useful adjectives: renewable energy (from the sun, wind, water); vulnerable people (easily harmed); humanitarian aid (help for people who are suffering); a growing concern; severe drought; widespread poverty; endangered species. Here are some examples. Governments must take action now to combat climate change. Our school campaign raised awareness of plastic pollution. Plastic waste poses a threat to sea turtles. Be careful! Some learners say: “We made awareness about water waste.” That’s not right. We say: “We raised awareness of water waste.” raise awareness of. Quick check: Do we \"make\" or \"raise\" awareness? … Think! … *raise* awareness. Great job! Now you can say: I can say \"tackle a problem\", \"raise awareness\" and \"reduce emissions\".","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"1.0"}]},{"id":"GV-L08-U2-LS4","title":"The Number of Refugees Is Rising: Subject–Verb Agreement with Tricky Subjects (SAT Form)","objectives":["Students will be able to find the real subject of a sentence and make the verb agree with it.","Students will be able to handle tricky subjects such as the number of, each of, neither… nor and collective nouns.","I can write \"The effects of climate change are serious.\"","I can choose between \"a number of people are\" and \"the number of people is\"."],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من تحديد الفاعل الحقيقي في الجملة وجعل الفعل يتفق معه.","سيتمكن الطلاب من التعامل مع الفواعل الصعبة مثل the number of وeach of وneither… nor والأسماء الجمعية.","أستطيع أن أكتب The effects of climate change are serious.","أستطيع أن أختار بين a number of people are وthe number of people is."],"vocabulary":[{"word":"crisis","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈkraɪsəs/","definition":"a time of great danger or difficulty","arabic":"أزمة","example":"The country faced an energy crisis.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"shortage","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈʃɔrtədʒ/","definition":"a situation in which there isn't enough of something","arabic":"نقص / شُحّ","example":"There is a shortage of clean water in many villages.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"emissions","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ɪˈmɪʃənz/","definition":"gases sent into the air, especially from cars and factories","arabic":"الانبعاثات","example":"Factories must reduce their carbon emissions.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"drought","pos":"noun","ipa":"/draʊt/","definition":"a long period with little or no rain","arabic":"جفاف","example":"The drought destroyed the farmers' crops.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"renewable","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/riˈnuəbəl/","definition":"coming from a source that does not run out, such as the sun or wind","arabic":"متجدّد","example":"Solar power is a renewable source of energy.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"conserve","pos":"verb","ipa":"/kənˈsɝv/","definition":"to use something carefully so it isn't wasted","arabic":"يحافظ على / يرشّد","example":"Turn off the tap to conserve water.","image_id":"","audio_id":""}],"explanation":{"text":"The verb agrees with the real subject, not with the noun closest to it. Cross out phrases between the subject and the verb: The effects (of climate change) are serious. The list (of endangered animals) is growing. as well as / along with / together with don't change the subject: The minister, along with his advisers, is visiting the camp.\nthe number of + plural noun → singular verb: The number of refugees is rising. a number of (= many) → plural: A number of students are volunteering. Collective nouns (team, government, committee, public, family) are usually singular in American English: The government has announced a new plan.\neach, every, everyone, nobody, neither, either → singular: Each of the countries has a plan. both, few, many, several → plural. some, most, all, none depend on the noun: Most of the water is wasted. Most of the rivers are polluted. With either… or / neither… nor, the verb agrees with the closer subject: Neither the minister nor the experts were available. In there is / there are, look after the verb: There are many causes. Nouns like news, physics, economics are singular: The news is good.\nfind the real subject – ignore phrases in between\nthe number of → singular • a number of → plural\neach / everyone / neither → singular • collective nouns → singular (AmE)\neither/neither … or/nor → agree with the closer subject","examples":["The causes of the drought are complex.","The number of plastic bags in the sea is shocking.","A number of volunteers have joined the campaign.","Each of the students has a different task.","The committee meets every Monday.","Neither the teachers nor the principal knows the answer.","There are several solutions to this problem.","The news about the rainforest is worrying."],"common_errors":["✗ The effects of climate change is serious. → ✓ The effects of climate change are serious. (Subject = effects (plural).)","✗ The number of refugees are rising. → ✓ The number of refugees is rising. (the number → singular.)","✗ Each of the countries have a plan. → ✓ Each of the countries has a plan. (each → singular.)","✗ The news are good today. → ✓ The news is good today. (news is singular.)"],"arabic":"الفعل يتفق مع الفاعل الحقيقي لا مع الاسم الأقرب: The effects of climate change are serious.\nthe number of + جمع ← فعل مفرد، وa number of (= كثير من) ← فعل جمع.\neach وeveryone وneither ← مفرد، والأسماء الجمعية (team, government) مفردة في الإنجليزية الأمريكية.\nمع either… or / neither… nor يتفق الفعل مع الأقرب، وnews وphysics مفردة. وهذه من أهم مهارات أسئلة Form, Structure, and Sense في SAT."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “The Number of Refugees Is Rising: Subject–Verb Agreement with Tricky Subjects (SAT Form)”. Let’s learn subject–verb agreement when a phrase comes between the subject and the verb; a number of vs the number of; collective nouns; indefinite pronouns (each, everyone, neither; both, many; some/most/all); either/neither…or/nor; there is/are; along with / as well as; nouns ending in -s (news, physics) together.","on_screen":"GV-L08-U2-LS4 | The Number of Refugees Is Rising: Subject–Verb Agreement with Tricky Subjects (SAT Form)","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"The verb agrees with the real subject, not with the noun closest to it. Cross out phrases between the subject and the verb: The effects (of climate change) are serious. The list (of endangered animals) is growing. as well as / along with / together with don't change the subject: The minister, along with his advisers, is visiting the camp.","on_screen":"subject–verb agreement when a phrase comes between the subject and the verb; a number of vs the number of; collective nouns; indefinite pronouns (each, everyone, neither; both, many; some/most/all); either/neither…or/nor; there is/are; along with / as well as; nouns ending in -s (news, physics)","visual":"Pattern strips slide in from the left; the key words are highlighted in Leaf Green."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"The verb agrees with the real subject, not with the noun closest to it. Cross out phrases between the subject and the verb: The effects (of climate change) are serious. The list (of endangered animals) is growing. as well as / along with / together with don't change the subject: The minister, along with his advisers, is visiting the camp. the number of + plural noun → singular verb: The number of refugees is rising. a number of (= many) → plural: A number of students are volunteering. Collective nouns (team, government, committee, public, family) are usually singular in American English: The government has announced a new plan.","on_screen":"find the real subject – ignore phrases in between • the number of → singular • a number of → plural • each / everyone / neither → singular • collective nouns → singular (AmE)","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. The causes of the drought are complex. The number of plastic bags in the sea is shocking. A number of volunteers have joined the campaign.","on_screen":"The causes of the drought are complex. / The number of plastic bags in the sea is shocking. / A number of volunteers have joined the campaign.","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “The effects of climate change is serious.” That’s not right. We say: “The effects of climate change are serious.” Subject = effects (plural).","on_screen":"✗ The effects of climate change is serious.   ✓ The effects of climate change are serious.","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:05","narration":"Quick check: \"The list of endangered animals ___ growing.\" What is the subject? … Think! … *list* – so *is*. Great job! Now you can say: I can write \"The effects of climate change are serious.\"","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can write \"The effects of climate change are serious.\"","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: subject–verb agreement when a phrase comes between the subject and the verb; a number of vs the number of; collective nouns; indefinite pronouns (each, everyone, neither; both, many; some/most/all); either/neither…or/nor; there is/are; along with / as well as; nouns ending in -s (news, physics).","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","الفعل يتفق مع الفاعل الحقيقي لا مع الاسم الأقرب: The effects of climate change are serious.","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: The effects of climate change is serious. — الصحيح: The effects of climate change are serious.","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أكتب The effects of climate change are serious."]},"texts":[{"type":"reading","title":"Water in Our Region (editing passage)","body":"The supply of fresh water in our region are limited. A number of farms uses too much water for crops. The number of wells have doubled in twenty years. Each of these wells take water from deep underground. The government have started a new campaign to save water.","word_count":48,"audio_id":""}],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L08-U2-LS4-A1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Controlled practice: Choose the correct verb.","items":[{"q":"The effects of plastic pollution ___ easy to see on our beaches.","options":["are","is","has been","was"],"answer":"are","explanation":"Ignore the phrase between the subject and the verb.","explanation_ar":"تجاهل العبارة الفاصلة."},{"q":"The number of refugees in the region ___ rising every year.","options":["have been","is","were","are"],"answer":"is","explanation":"the number of (singular) / a number of (plural).","explanation_ar":"the number / a number."},{"q":"A number of students ___ volunteering at the food bank this weekend.","options":["was","has","is","are"],"answer":"are","explanation":"the number of (singular) / a number of (plural).","explanation_ar":"the number / a number."},{"q":"The government ___ announced a new water-saving plan.","options":["are","were","has","have"],"answer":"has","explanation":"Collective nouns → singular (American English).","explanation_ar":"الأسماء الجمعية."},{"q":"Each of the participating countries ___ a different plan to reduce emissions.","options":["were","are","has","have"],"answer":"has","explanation":"each / everyone / neither → singular; both / many → plural.","explanation_ar":"الضمائر غير المحددة."},{"q":"The collection of rare seeds stored in the Svalbard Global Seed Vault in Norway ______ designed to protect crops from future disasters.\n\nWhich choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","options":["are","were","have been","is"],"answer":"is","explanation":"Ignore the phrase between the subject and the verb.","explanation_ar":"تجاهل العبارة الفاصلة."}]},{"id":"GV-L08-U2-LS4-B1","type":"gap_fill","instructions":"Guided practice: Complete with is, are, has or have. Word bank: are, is, knows","items":[{"q":"Neither the teachers nor the principal ______ (know) the answer yet.","options":[],"answer":"knows","explanation":"either/neither … or/nor → the closer subject.","explanation_ar":"الأقرب إلى الفعل."},{"q":"There ______ (be) several causes of the water crisis.","options":[],"answer":"are","explanation":"there is / there are → look after the verb.","explanation_ar":"there is / are."},{"q":"The news about the coral reefs ______ (be) worrying.","options":[],"answer":"is","explanation":"there is / there are → look after the verb.","explanation_ar":"there is / are."}]},{"id":"GV-L08-U2-LS4-B2","type":"open","instructions":"Guided practice: Correct the mistake.","items":[{"q":"The list of endangered animals are getting longer.","options":[],"answer":"The list of endangered animals is getting longer.","explanation":"are → is. Ignore the phrase between the subject and the verb.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: are → is. تجاهل العبارة الفاصلة."},{"q":"The minister, along with his advisers, are visiting the camp today.","options":[],"answer":"The minister, along with his advisers, is visiting the camp today.","explanation":"are → is. Ignore the phrase between the subject and the verb.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: are → is. تجاهل العبارة الفاصلة."},{"q":"Everyone in the villages need clean water.","options":[],"answer":"Everyone in the villages needs clean water.","explanation":"need → needs. each / everyone / neither → singular; both / many → plural.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: need → needs. الضمائر غير المحددة."}]},{"id":"GV-L08-U2-LS4-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Edit the report.","items":[{"q":"The supply of fresh water in our region are limited.","options":[],"answer":"The supply of fresh water in our region is limited.","explanation":"are → is. Ignore the phrase between the subject and the verb.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: are → is. تجاهل العبارة الفاصلة."},{"q":"A number of farms uses too much water for crops.","options":[],"answer":"A number of farms use too much water for crops.","explanation":"uses → use. Ignore the phrase between the subject and the verb.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: uses → use. تجاهل العبارة الفاصلة."},{"q":"The number of wells have doubled in twenty years.","options":[],"answer":"The number of wells has doubled in twenty years.","explanation":"have → has. Ignore the phrase between the subject and the verb.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: have → has. تجاهل العبارة الفاصلة."},{"q":"Each of these wells take water from deep underground.","options":[],"answer":"Each of these wells takes water from deep underground.","explanation":"take → takes. Ignore the phrase between the subject and the verb.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: take → takes. تجاهل العبارة الفاصلة."},{"q":"The number of wells have doubled in twenty years.","options":[],"answer":"The number of wells has doubled in twenty years.","explanation":"have → has. Ignore the phrase between the subject and the verb.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: have → has. تجاهل العبارة الفاصلة."}]},{"id":"GV-L08-U2-LS4-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: Write correct sentences.","items":[{"q":"Write a sentence beginning with \"The number of…\".","options":[],"answer":"The number of electric cars in Saudi Arabia is increasing.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses subject–verb agreement when a phrase comes between the subject and the verb; a number of vs the number of; collective nouns; indefinite pronouns (each, everyone, neither; both, many; some/most/all); either/neither…or/nor; there is/are; along with / as well as; nouns ending in -s (news, physics) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write a sentence beginning with \"A number of…\".","options":[],"answer":"A number of companies are investing in solar energy.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses subject–verb agreement when a phrase comes between the subject and the verb; a number of vs the number of; collective nouns; indefinite pronouns (each, everyone, neither; both, many; some/most/all); either/neither…or/nor; there is/are; along with / as well as; nouns ending in -s (news, physics) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write a sentence with \"Each of…\" about global issues.","options":[],"answer":"Each of the world's oceans is affected by plastic pollution.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses subject–verb agreement when a phrase comes between the subject and the verb; a number of vs the number of; collective nouns; indefinite pronouns (each, everyone, neither; both, many; some/most/all); either/neither…or/nor; there is/are; along with / as well as; nouns ending in -s (news, physics) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Letter Ladder","mechanic":"word_builder","rules":["The leader chooses a word from the list and draws one blank line per letter.","Teams take turns guessing letters. Correct letters are written on the lines.","Each wrong guess removes one rung of the ladder (start with 6 rungs).","The team that completes the word scores 2 points and uses it in a sentence."],"data":[{"word":"emissions","clue":"gases sent into the air, especially from cars and factories"},{"word":"renewable","clue":"coming from a source that does not run out, such as the sun or wind"},{"word":"humanitarian","clue":"concerned with helping people who are suffering"},{"word":"vulnerable","clue":"easily hurt or harmed"},{"word":"biodiversity","clue":"the variety of plants and animals in a place"},{"word":"deforestation","clue":"cutting down large areas of forest"},{"word":"crisis","clue":"a time of great danger or difficulty"},{"word":"shortage","clue":"a situation in which there isn't enough of something"},{"word":"drought","clue":"a long period with little or no rain"},{"word":"conserve","clue":"to use something carefully so it isn't wasted"},{"word":"poverty","clue":"the state of being very poor"},{"word":"refugee","clue":"a person who has to leave his country because of war or disaster"}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"The causes of the forest fire ___ still unknown.","options":["was","has been","are","is"],"answer":"are","explanation":"Ignore the phrase between the subject and the verb.","explanation_ar":"تجاهل العبارة الفاصلة."},{"q":"The number of electric cars on the roads ___ increasing quickly.","options":["have","were","is","are"],"answer":"is","explanation":"the number of (singular) / a number of (plural).","explanation_ar":"the number / a number."},{"q":"A number of countries ___ promised to plant more trees.","options":["have","is","was","has"],"answer":"have","explanation":"the number of (singular) / a number of (plural).","explanation_ar":"the number / a number."},{"q":"The committee ___ every Sunday to discuss the project.","options":["are meeting","meets","have met","meet"],"answer":"meets","explanation":"Collective nouns → singular (American English).","explanation_ar":"الأسماء الجمعية."},{"q":"Neither the doctors nor the nurse ___ been told about the new rule.","options":["have","were","are","has"],"answer":"has","explanation":"either/neither … or/nor → the closer subject.","explanation_ar":"الأقرب إلى الفعل."},{"q":"There ___ a lot of plastic on the beach after the storm.","options":["are","was","have been","were"],"answer":"was","explanation":"there is / there are → look after the verb.","explanation_ar":"there is / are."},{"q":"","options":["Physics is my brother's favorite subject.","Physics were my brother's favorite subject.","Physics are my brother's favorite subject.","Physics have been my brother's favorite subject."],"answer":"Physics is my brother's favorite subject.","explanation":"there is / there are → look after the verb.","explanation_ar":"there is / are."},{"q":"The tiny islands that make up the Maldives, a country in the Indian Ocean, ______ especially vulnerable to rising sea levels.\n\nWhich choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","options":["has been","is","was","are"],"answer":"are","explanation":"Ignore the phrase between the subject and the verb.","explanation_ar":"تجاهل العبارة الفاصلة."},{"q":"According to recent research, each of the world's major coral reef systems ______ been affected by rising ocean temperatures.\n\nWhich choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","options":["are","were","have","has"],"answer":"has","explanation":"each / everyone / neither → singular; both / many → plural.","explanation_ar":"الضمائر غير المحددة."},{"q":"Either the students or their teacher ______ going to present the results at the conference.\n\nWhich choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","options":["are","were","is","have"],"answer":"is","explanation":"either/neither … or/nor → the closer subject.","explanation_ar":"الأقرب إلى الفعل."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L08-U2-LS4-IMG01","prompt":"Two or three of the programme characters in a scene about “Global Challenges” that shows subject–verb agreement when a phrase comes between the subject and the verb; a number of vs the number of; collective nouns; indefinite pronouns (each, everyone, neither; both, many; some/most/all); either/neither…or/nor; there is/are; along with / as well as; nouns ending in -s (news, physics) in action. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"Two or three of the programme characters in a scene about “Global Challenges” that shows subject–verb agreement when a phrase comes between the subject and the verb; a number of vs the number of; collective nouns; indefinite pronouns (each, everyone, neither; both, many; some/most/all); either/neither…or/nor; there is/are; along with / as well as; nouns ending in -s (news, physics) in action"},{"id":"GV-L08-U2-LS4-IMG02","prompt":"friendly editing-desk scene: a magnifying glass over a page with highlighted punctuation marks, Zaki holding a green pen. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"friendly editing-desk scene: a magnifying glass over a page with highlighted punctuation marks, Zaki holding a green pen"},{"id":"GV-L08-U2-LS4-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Letter Ladder”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Letter Ladder"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L08-U2-LS4-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “The Number of Refugees Is Rising: Subject–Verb Agreement with Tricky Subjects (SAT Form)”. Let’s learn subject–verb agreement when a phrase comes between the subject and the verb; a number of vs the number of; collective nouns; indefinite pronouns (each, everyone, neither; both, many; some/most/all); either/neither…or/nor; there is/are; along with / as well as; nouns ending in -s (news, physics) together. The verb agrees with the real subject, not with the noun closest to it. Cross out phrases between the subject and the verb: The effects (of climate change) are serious. The list (of endangered animals) is growing. as well as / along with / together with don't change the subject: The minister, along with his advisers, is visiting the camp. The verb agrees with the real subject, not with the noun closest to it. Cross out phrases between the subject and the verb: The effects (of climate change) are serious. The list (of endangered animals) is growing. as well as / along with / together with don't change the subject: The minister, along with his advisers, is visiting the camp. the number of + plural noun → singular verb: The number of refugees is rising. a number of (= many) → plural: A number of students are volunteering. Collective nouns (team, government, committee, public, family) are usually singular in American English: The government has announced a new plan. Here are some examples. The causes of the drought are complex. The number of plastic bags in the sea is shocking. A number of volunteers have joined the campaign. Be careful! Some learners say: “The effects of climate change is serious.” That’s not right. We say: “The effects of climate change are serious.” Subject = effects (plural). Quick check: \"The list of endangered animals ___ growing.\" What is the subject? … Think! … *list* – so *is*. Great job! Now you can say: I can write \"The effects of climate change are serious.\"","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"1.0"}]},{"id":"GV-L08-U2-LS5","title":"A Letter About Water Waste: Language in Use","objectives":["Students will be able to discuss a global issue formally in a group debate.","Students will be able to write a formal letter about a global issue with the impersonal passive, collocations and correct agreement, and answer SAT-style transition and synthesis items.","I can give a formal opinion about a global problem.","I can write a letter to a newspaper editor."],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من مناقشة قضية عالمية بأسلوب رسمي في مناظرة جماعية.","سيتمكن الطلاب من كتابة رسالة رسمية عن قضية عالمية بالمبني للمجهول غير الشخصي والمتلازمات والاتفاق الصحيح، والإجابة عن أسئلة الروابط والتركيب بنمط SAT.","أستطيع أن أعطي رأيًا رسميًّا في مشكلة عالمية.","أستطيع أن أكتب رسالة إلى محرر صحيفة."],"vocabulary":[{"word":"crisis","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈkraɪsəs/","definition":"a time of great danger or difficulty","arabic":"أزمة","example":"The country faced an energy crisis.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"shortage","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈʃɔrtədʒ/","definition":"a situation in which there isn't enough of something","arabic":"نقص / شُحّ","example":"There is a shortage of clean water in many villages.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"emissions","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ɪˈmɪʃənz/","definition":"gases sent into the air, especially from cars and factories","arabic":"الانبعاثات","example":"Factories must reduce their carbon emissions.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"drought","pos":"noun","ipa":"/draʊt/","definition":"a long period with little or no rain","arabic":"جفاف","example":"The drought destroyed the farmers' crops.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"renewable","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/riˈnuəbəl/","definition":"coming from a source that does not run out, such as the sun or wind","arabic":"متجدّد","example":"Solar power is a renewable source of energy.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"conserve","pos":"verb","ipa":"/kənˈsɝv/","definition":"to use something carefully so it isn't wasted","arabic":"يحافظ على / يرشّد","example":"Turn off the tap to conserve water.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"poverty","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈpɑvɚti/","definition":"the state of being very poor","arabic":"الفقر","example":"Education helps families escape poverty.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"refugee","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈrɛfjudʒi/","definition":"a person who has to leave his country because of war or disaster","arabic":"لاجئ","example":"The camp gave shelter to thousands of refugees.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"deforestation","pos":"noun","ipa":"/dɪˌfɔrɪˈsteɪʃən/","definition":"cutting down large areas of forest","arabic":"إزالة الغابات","example":"Deforestation destroys the homes of many animals.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"humanitarian","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/ˌhjuˌmænəˈtɛriən/","definition":"concerned with helping people who are suffering","arabic":"إنساني","example":"The organization sent humanitarian aid after the flood.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"vulnerable","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/ˈvʌlnɚəbəl/","definition":"easily hurt or harmed","arabic":"ضعيف / معرَّض للخطر","example":"Children and the elderly are the most vulnerable in a heat wave.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"inequality","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˌɪnɪˈkwɑləti/","definition":"an unfair situation in which some people have more opportunities than others","arabic":"عدم المساواة","example":"Inequality in education is a global problem.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"tackle","pos":"verb","ipa":"/ˈtækəl/","definition":"to make a serious effort to deal with a problem","arabic":"يعالج / يتصدّى لـ","example":"Governments must work together to tackle climate change.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"contaminate","pos":"verb","ipa":"/kənˈtæməˌneɪt/","definition":"to make water, food or air dirty or harmful","arabic":"يلوّث","example":"Chemicals from the factory contaminated the river.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"biodiversity","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˌbaɪoʊdaɪˈvɝsəti/","definition":"the variety of plants and animals in a place","arabic":"التنوع الحيوي","example":"Coral reefs are rich in biodiversity.","image_id":"","audio_id":""}],"explanation":{"text":"Today you use all of Unit 2: the impersonal passive (It is said that… / X is known to…), passive infinitives (needs to be tackled), global-issue collocations and subject–verb agreement.\nA formal letter states the issue, gives evidence (often with It is estimated that…), explains why it matters, and suggests action. SAT Expression of Ideas items test the same thinking: which transition shows the right relationship, and which sentence best uses evidence for a specific goal.\n✔ It is said / estimated that… • X is known / believed to…\n✔ needs to be done • is expected to be done\n✔ raise awareness, take action, pose a threat, tackle a problem\n✔ the number of → is • each of → has • a number of → are","examples":["It is estimated that a dripping tap wastes thousands of liters a year.","Leaking pipes need to be repaired quickly.","The number of water-saving devices in homes is still low.","A number of schools have started recycling programs.","We must take action before the problem gets worse.","The campaign aims to raise awareness of water waste.","Desalination plants are known to use a great deal of energy.","Each of us has a role to play."],"common_errors":["✗ It is said water is life. (formal letter) → ✓ It is often said that water is life. (Use the full formal pattern.)","✗ The problem needs to tackle by everyone. → ✓ The problem needs to be tackled by everyone. (Passive infinitive.)","✗ Each of these habits seem harmless. → ✓ Each of these habits seems harmless. (each → singular.)"],"arabic":"نراجع المبني للمجهول غير الشخصي والمصدر المبني للمجهول ومتلازمات القضايا العالمية واتفاق الفاعل والفعل.\nالرسالة الرسمية تعرض المشكلة، وتقدّم الأدلة، وتشرح أهميتها، وتقترح حلولًا.\nأسئلة SAT في Expression of Ideas تختبر المهارة نفسها: اختيار الرابط المناسب، واختيار الجملة التي تستخدم الأدلة لتحقيق هدف محدد."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “A Letter About Water Waste: Language in Use”. Let’s learn impersonal passive and passive infinitives, global-issue collocations, subject–verb agreement; SAT transitions and rhetorical synthesis (unit review) together.","on_screen":"GV-L08-U2-LS5 | A Letter About Water Waste: Language in Use","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"Let’s use everything from this unit. Your task: Mini Model UN: groups represent four \"countries\". Each group gives a 1-minute statement on water shortage with two impersonal passive sentences, one passive infinitive (needs to be done) and two global-issue collocations. The class votes on the best plan.","on_screen":"Language in use","visual":"Split screen: two cast members talking, with speech bubbles appearing."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"Today you use all of Unit 2: the impersonal passive (It is said that… / X is known to…), passive infinitives (needs to be tackled), global-issue collocations and subject–verb agreement. A formal letter states the issue, gives evidence (often with It is estimated that…), explains why it matters, and suggests action. SAT Expression of Ideas items test the same thinking: which transition shows the right relationship, and which sentence best uses evidence for a specific goal.","on_screen":"✔ It is said / estimated that… • X is known / believed to… • ✔ needs to be done • is expected to be done • ✔ raise awareness, take action, pose a threat, tackle a problem","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. It is estimated that a dripping tap wastes thousands of liters a year. Leaking pipes need to be repaired quickly. The number of water-saving devices in homes is still low.","on_screen":"It is estimated that a dripping tap wastes thousands of liters a year. / Leaking pipes need to be repaired quickly. / The number of water-saving devices in homes is still low.","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “It is said water is life. (formal letter).” That’s not right. We say: “It is often said that water is life.” Use the full formal pattern.","on_screen":"✗ It is said water is life. (formal letter)   ✓ It is often said that water is life.","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:05","narration":"Quick check: what is wrong with “The problem needs to tackle by everyone.”? … Think! … It should be “The problem needs to be tackled by everyone.”. Great job! Now you can say: I can give a formal opinion about a global problem.","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can give a formal opinion about a global problem.","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: impersonal passive and passive infinitives, global-issue collocations, subject–verb agreement; SAT transitions and rhetorical synthesis (unit review).","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","نراجع المبني للمجهول غير الشخصي والمصدر المبني للمجهول ومتلازمات القضايا العالمية واتفاق الفاعل والفعل.","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: It is said water is life. (formal letter) — الصحيح: It is often said that water is life.","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أعطي رأيًا رسميًّا في مشكلة عالمية."]},"texts":[{"type":"model","title":"Letter to the Editor – Faisal","body":"Dear Editor,\nIt is often said that water is life, yet many of us waste it every day.\nIn our city, a large number of households still water their gardens at noon, when most of the water evaporates.\nEach of these small habits seems harmless, but together they pose a serious threat to our future.\nSaudi Arabia is known to be one of the world's largest producers of desalinated water; however, desalination is expensive and uses a great deal of energy.\nThe problem needs to be tackled by everyone, not only by the government.\nI believe that schools should raise awareness, and families should take action at home.\nSincerely,\nFaisal","word_count":110,"audio_id":"AUD-GV-L08-U2-LS5-T1"}],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L08-U2-LS5-A1","type":"true_false","instructions":"Controlled practice: Read Faisal's letter. True or False?","items":[{"q":"Faisal thinks that very few people waste water.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"False","explanation":"Check the text “Letter to the Editor – Faisal”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"Many households water their gardens at noon.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"True","explanation":"Check the text “Letter to the Editor – Faisal”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"Faisal believes small habits can add up to a serious threat.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"True","explanation":"Check the text “Letter to the Editor – Faisal”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"According to the letter, desalination is cheap and uses little energy.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"False","explanation":"Check the text “Letter to the Editor – Faisal”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"Faisal thinks only the government should tackle the problem.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"False","explanation":"Check the text “Letter to the Editor – Faisal”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"He suggests that schools should raise awareness.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"True","explanation":"Check the text “Letter to the Editor – Faisal”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."}]},{"id":"GV-L08-U2-LS5-B1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Guided practice: Choose the correct answer.","items":[{"q":"It is often ___ that water is life.","options":["say","saying","to say","said"],"answer":"said","explanation":"Impersonal passive or passive infinitive.","explanation_ar":"المبني للمجهول."},{"q":"Saudi Arabia is known ___ one of the largest producers of desalinated water.","options":["to have being","to be","that it is","being"],"answer":"to be","explanation":"Impersonal passive or passive infinitive.","explanation_ar":"المبني للمجهول."},{"q":"Each of these small habits ___ harmless.","options":["seems","seem","are seeming","have seemed"],"answer":"seems","explanation":"Subject–verb agreement.","explanation_ar":"اتفاق الفاعل والفعل."},{"q":"Together, these habits ___ a serious threat to our future.","options":["do","raise","pose","make"],"answer":"pose","explanation":"Global-issue collocation.","explanation_ar":"المتلازمة."},{"q":"The problem needs ___ by everyone.","options":["to have tackle","to be tackled","to tackle","tackling it"],"answer":"to be tackled","explanation":"Impersonal passive or passive infinitive.","explanation_ar":"المبني للمجهول."},{"q":"Desalination provides most of Saudi Arabia's drinking water. ______ it is expensive and uses a great deal of energy.\n\nWhich choice completes the text with the most logical transition?","options":["Similarly,","Therefore,","However,","For example,"],"answer":"However,","explanation":"Logical transition.","explanation_ar":"الرابط المنطقي."}]},{"id":"GV-L08-U2-LS5-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Prepare your Model UN statement.","items":[{"q":"Your country and the issue: ___","options":[],"answer":"Our country is facing a severe water shortage.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses impersonal passive and passive infinitives, global-issue collocations, subject–verb agreement; SAT transitions and rhetorical synthesis (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"One impersonal passive sentence with evidence: ___","options":[],"answer":"It is estimated that our rivers have lost half their water in thirty years.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses impersonal passive and passive infinitives, global-issue collocations, subject–verb agreement; SAT transitions and rhetorical synthesis (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"One sentence with \"needs to be…\": ___","options":[],"answer":"Agriculture needs to be modernized to use less water.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses impersonal passive and passive infinitives, global-issue collocations, subject–verb agreement; SAT transitions and rhetorical synthesis (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Two collocations you will use: ___","options":[],"answer":"take action, raise awareness","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses impersonal passive and passive infinitives, global-issue collocations, subject–verb agreement; SAT transitions and rhetorical synthesis (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"A sentence with \"The number of…\" or \"A number of…\": ___","options":[],"answer":"The number of farms using drip irrigation is still very small.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses impersonal passive and passive infinitives, global-issue collocations, subject–verb agreement; SAT transitions and rhetorical synthesis (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]},{"id":"GV-L08-U2-LS5-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: Write your letter to the editor.","items":[{"q":"Plan: issue, evidence, why it matters, two actions, greeting and closing.","options":[],"answer":"food waste in restaurants; it is estimated that a third of food is wasted; poses a threat to the environment; restaurants need to donate leftovers; families should plan meals; Dear Editor, / Sincerely,","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses impersonal passive and passive infinitives, global-issue collocations, subject–verb agreement; SAT transitions and rhetorical synthesis (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write your letter in 8–9 sentences.","options":[],"answer":"Dear Editor, It is estimated that about a third of the world's food is wasted. In our city, a number of restaurants throw away large amounts of food every night. Each of these meals represents water, energy and work. Food waste is also known to produce harmful gases in landfills. This problem needs to be tackled urgently. Restaurants should donate leftovers to charities. Families can take action by planning their meals carefully. Together, we can raise awareness and make a difference. Sincerely, Saad","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses impersonal passive and passive infinitives, global-issue collocations, subject–verb agreement; SAT transitions and rhetorical synthesis (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Check: impersonal passive? passive infinitives? agreement with tricky subjects? Fix one mistake.","options":[],"answer":"I changed \"A number of restaurants throws\" to \"A number of restaurants throw\".","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses impersonal passive and passive infinitives, global-issue collocations, subject–verb agreement; SAT transitions and rhetorical synthesis (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Treasure Hunt Review","mechanic":"timed_quiz","rules":["Teams move to a station every 90 seconds.","At each station, write one correct sentence with the cue word and impersonal passive and passive infinitives, global-issue collocations, subject–verb agreement; SAT transitions and rhetorical synthesis (unit review).","Teams collect a \"treasure letter\" for each correct sentence.","Unscramble the letters at the end to reveal the secret word."],"data":[{"cue":"crisis","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"shortage","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"emissions","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"drought","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"renewable","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"conserve","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"poverty","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"refugee","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"deforestation","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"humanitarian","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"vulnerable","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"inequality","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"tackle","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"contaminate","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"biodiversity","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"It ___ that one third of the world's food is wasted.","options":["estimates","has estimate","is estimating","is estimated"],"answer":"is estimated","explanation":"Impersonal passive or passive infinitive.","explanation_ar":"المبني للمجهول."},{"q":"The leftovers need ___ to people in need.","options":["to be given","giving to","to have give","to give them"],"answer":"to be given","explanation":"Impersonal passive or passive infinitive.","explanation_ar":"المبني للمجهول."},{"q":"The number of students who walk to school ___ increased this year.","options":["have","has","were","are"],"answer":"has","explanation":"Subject–verb agreement.","explanation_ar":"اتفاق الفاعل والفعل."},{"q":"A number of local businesses ___ joined the recycling campaign.","options":["has","have","is","was"],"answer":"have","explanation":"Subject–verb agreement.","explanation_ar":"اتفاق الفاعل والفعل."},{"q":"The campaign helped to ___ awareness of food waste.","options":["rise","do","raise","make"],"answer":"raise","explanation":"Global-issue collocation.","explanation_ar":"المتلازمة."},{"q":"","options":["Everyone in the neighborhood have a part to play.","Everyone in the neighborhood were a part to play.","Everyone in the neighborhood are having a part to play.","Everyone in the neighborhood has a part to play."],"answer":"Everyone in the neighborhood has a part to play.","explanation":"Subject–verb agreement.","explanation_ar":"اتفاق الفاعل والفعل."},{"q":"Many cities have banned single-use plastic bags. ______ shoppers in those cities now carry reusable bags.\n\nWhich choice completes the text with the most logical transition?","options":["As a result,","In contrast,","Nevertheless,","However,"],"answer":"As a result,","explanation":"Logical transition.","explanation_ar":"الرابط المنطقي."},{"q":"Some solutions to the water crisis are very expensive. ______ fixing leaking pipes costs little and can save millions of liters.\n\nWhich choice completes the text with the most logical transition?","options":["Likewise,","Therefore,","In contrast,","For example,"],"answer":"In contrast,","explanation":"Logical transition.","explanation_ar":"الرابط المنطقي."},{"q":"While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:\n• Mangrove forests grow along the Red Sea and the Arabian Gulf.\n• Mangroves protect coasts from storms and erosion.\n• They store large amounts of carbon.\n• Saudi Arabia has planted millions of mangrove trees in recent years.\n\nThe student wants to explain why planting mangroves helps fight climate change. Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","options":["Mangroves protect coasts from storms and erosion.","Because mangroves store large amounts of carbon, planting millions of them helps reduce the gases that cause climate change.","Saudi Arabia has planted mangrove trees, which grow near the sea.","Mangrove forests grow along the Red Sea and the Arabian Gulf."],"answer":"Because mangroves store large amounts of carbon, planting millions of them helps reduce the gases that cause climate change.","explanation":"Rhetorical synthesis.","explanation_ar":"التركيب البلاغي."},{"q":"While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:\n• Desalination removes salt from seawater.\n• It produces fresh drinking water.\n• Traditional desalination plants use a lot of energy.\n• New plants in Saudi Arabia use solar power.\n\nThe student wants to present a solution to the energy problem of desalination. Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","options":["Desalination removes salt from seawater.","Desalination produces fresh drinking water for many people.","Although traditional desalination uses a lot of energy, new Saudi plants reduce this problem by using solar power.","Traditional desalination plants use a lot of energy."],"answer":"Although traditional desalination uses a lot of energy, new Saudi plants reduce this problem by using solar power.","explanation":"Rhetorical synthesis.","explanation_ar":"التركيب البلاغي."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L08-U2-LS5-IMG01","prompt":"Faisal at a desk writing a letter to a newspaper, with a window view of sprinklers watering a garden at noon under a blazing sun; a newspaper page titled \"Letters to the Editor\". Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"Faisal at a desk writing a letter to a newspaper, with a window view of sprinklers watering a garden at noon under a blazing sun; a newspaper page titled \"Letters to the Editor\""},{"id":"GV-L08-U2-LS5-IMG02","prompt":"two programme characters doing the speaking task about “Global Challenges”, speech bubbles left empty. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"two programme characters doing the speaking task about “Global Challenges”, speech bubbles left empty"},{"id":"GV-L08-U2-LS5-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Treasure Hunt Review”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Treasure Hunt Review"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L08-U2-LS5-T1","script":"Dear Editor, It is often said that water is life, yet many of us waste it every day. In our city, a large number of households still water their gardens at noon, when most of the water evaporates. Each of these small habits seems harmless, but together they pose a serious threat to our future. Saudi Arabia is known to be one of the world's largest producers of desalinated water; however, desalination is expensive and uses a great deal of energy. The problem needs to be tackled by everyone, not only by the government. I believe that schools should raise awareness, and families should take action at home. Sincerely, Faisal","voice":"en-US, natural young-adult voice","speed":"1.0"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L08-U2-LS5-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “A Letter About Water Waste: Language in Use”. Let’s learn impersonal passive and passive infinitives, global-issue collocations, subject–verb agreement; SAT transitions and rhetorical synthesis (unit review) together. Let’s use everything from this unit. Your task: Mini Model UN: groups represent four \"countries\". Each group gives a 1-minute statement on water shortage with two impersonal passive sentences, one passive infinitive (needs to be done) and two global-issue collocations. The class votes on the best plan. Today you use all of Unit 2: the impersonal passive (It is said that… / X is known to…), passive infinitives (needs to be tackled), global-issue collocations and subject–verb agreement. A formal letter states the issue, gives evidence (often with It is estimated that…), explains why it matters, and suggests action. SAT Expression of Ideas items test the same thinking: which transition shows the right relationship, and which sentence best uses evidence for a specific goal. Here are some examples. It is estimated that a dripping tap wastes thousands of liters a year. Leaking pipes need to be repaired quickly. The number of water-saving devices in homes is still low. Be careful! Some learners say: “It is said water is life. (formal letter).” That’s not right. We say: “It is often said that water is life.” Use the full formal pattern. Quick check: what is wrong with “The problem needs to tackle by everyone.”? … Think! … It should be “The problem needs to be tackled by everyone.”. Great job! Now you can say: I can give a formal opinion about a global problem.","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"1.0"}]}],"unit_test":[{"q":"___ that the city's population will double by 2040.","options":["It is expecting","They are expected","It expects","It is expected"],"answer":"It is expected","explanation":"It + is + reporting verb (past participle) + that.","explanation_ar":"النمط It is said that."},{"q":"The old fort is believed ___ over 200 years old.","options":["to be","to have being","that it is","being"],"answer":"to be","explanation":"Subject + is + reporting verb + to-infinitive.","explanation_ar":"النمط Subject + is said to."},{"q":"The earthquake is thought ___ more than 500 buildings.","options":["that damaged","damaging","to damage","to have damaged"],"answer":"to have damaged","explanation":"Earlier action → to have + past participle.","explanation_ar":"الحدث الأسبق ← to have done."},{"q":"Glaciers in the Himalayas are reported ___ faster than ever.","options":["melting to be","to be melting","that they melt","to melt yesterday"],"answer":"to be melting","explanation":"Action in progress → to be + -ing.","explanation_ar":"الحدث الجاري ← to be doing."},{"q":"","options":["The Nabataeans are known that they built Hegra.","It is known that the Nabataeans built Hegra.","It knows that the Nabataeans built Hegra.","It is knowing that the Nabataeans built Hegra."],"answer":"It is known that the Nabataeans built Hegra.","explanation":"Don't mix the two patterns.","explanation_ar":"لا خلط بين النمطين."},{"q":"The broken water pipes need ___ before summer.","options":["repairing it","to repair","to be repaired","to have repair"],"answer":"to be repaired","explanation":"need / want / expect / deserve + passive infinitive.","explanation_ar":"الأفعال قبل المصدر المجهول."},{"q":"The bridge is expected ___ by the end of next year.","options":["to have completed last","completing","to be completed","to complete"],"answer":"to be completed","explanation":"to be + past participle (now/future).","explanation_ar":"to be done."},{"q":"The ancient scrolls are believed ___ in the cave for centuries.","options":["to have been hidden","to hide","to have hidden","hiding"],"answer":"to have been hidden","explanation":"to have been + past participle (earlier).","explanation_ar":"to have been done."},{"q":"Every child deserves ___ to school.","options":["to be sent","to have sent","to send","sending"],"answer":"to be sent","explanation":"need / want / expect / deserve + passive infinitive.","explanation_ar":"الأفعال قبل المصدر المجهول."},{"q":"The Svalbard Global Seed Vault, built inside a mountain in Norway, ______ to protect over a million types of seeds from disasters.\n\nWhich choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","options":["are designed","design","have been designing","is designed"],"answer":"is designed","explanation":"Ignore the phrase between the subject and the verb.","explanation_ar":"تجاهل العبارة الفاصلة."},{"q":"Volunteers worked all weekend to ___ awareness of the dangers of littering.","options":["do","raise","rise","make"],"answer":"raise","explanation":"Use the right collocation.","explanation_ar":"المتلازمة الصحيحة."},{"q":"Rising temperatures ___ a serious threat to coral reefs.","options":["pose","take","do","make"],"answer":"pose","explanation":"Use the right collocation.","explanation_ar":"المتلازمة الصحيحة."},{"q":"People who leave their country because of war are ___.","options":["volunteers","merchants","refugees","emissions"],"answer":"refugees","explanation":"Who does the action?","explanation_ar":"مَن يقوم بالفعل؟"},{"q":"The farmers' wells dried up after three years of ___.","options":["flood","shortage","crisis","drought"],"answer":"drought","explanation":"Who does the action?","explanation_ar":"مَن يقوم بالفعل؟"},{"q":"The organization sends ___ aid to areas hit by disasters.","options":["renewable","contaminated","humanitarian","vulnerable"],"answer":"humanitarian","explanation":"Choose the precise adjective.","explanation_ar":"الصفة الدقيقة."},{"q":"Scientists warn that if the rainforest continues to shrink, many species will lose their habitats, and the region's rich ______ will be lost forever.\n\nWhich choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","options":["inequality","biodiversity","drought","poverty"],"answer":"biodiversity","explanation":"Who does the action?","explanation_ar":"مَن يقوم بالفعل؟"},{"q":"The causes of the water shortage ___ complicated.","options":["was","are","is","has been"],"answer":"are","explanation":"Ignore the phrase between the subject and the verb.","explanation_ar":"تجاهل العبارة الفاصلة."},{"q":"The number of people living in cities ___ growing fast.","options":["are","have","were","is"],"answer":"is","explanation":"the number of (singular) / a number of (plural).","explanation_ar":"the number / a number."},{"q":"Each of the volunteers ___ a certificate at the end of the project.","options":["receive","are receiving","have received","receives"],"answer":"receives","explanation":"each / everyone / neither → singular; both / many → plural.","explanation_ar":"الضمائر غير المحددة."},{"q":"","options":["The news from the conference is encouraging.","The news from the conference have been encouraging.","The news from the conference were encouraging.","The news from the conference are encouraging."],"answer":"The news from the conference is encouraging.","explanation":"there is / there are → look after the verb.","explanation_ar":"there is / are."},{"q":"The team of engineers that designed the new solar plant in the desert ______ won an international award for its work.\n\nWhich choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","options":["have","has","were","are"],"answer":"has","explanation":"Collective nouns → singular (American English).","explanation_ar":"الأسماء الجمعية."},{"q":"Many coastal cities are building sea walls to protect themselves from floods. ______ the Netherlands has protected its low-lying land with a huge system of dams and sea walls.\n\nWhich choice completes the text with the most logical transition?","options":["For example,","Nevertheless,","Instead,","However,"],"answer":"For example,","explanation":"Logical transition.","explanation_ar":"الرابط المنطقي."},{"q":"While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:\n• The Saudi Green Initiative was announced in 2021.\n• It aims to plant ten billion trees in Saudi Arabia.\n• Trees can reduce dust storms.\n• Trees help protect the soil.\n\nThe student wants to describe the environmental benefits of the initiative. Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","options":["The Saudi Green Initiative was announced in 2021.","Saudi Arabia announced a new initiative about trees.","By planting ten billion trees, the Saudi Green Initiative aims to reduce dust storms and protect the soil.","The initiative was announced, and it is about ten billion trees."],"answer":"By planting ten billion trees, the Saudi Green Initiative aims to reduce dust storms and protect the soil.","explanation":"Rhetorical synthesis.","explanation_ar":"التركيب البلاغي."},{"q":"How can we fix it? \"the number of plastic bottles in the sea are believed to rise.\"","options":["The number of plastic bottles in the sea is believed that it rises.","The number of plastic bottles in the sea are believed to be rising.","The number of plastic bottles in the sea is believed to be rising.","the number of plastic bottles in the sea is believed to be rising."],"answer":"The number of plastic bottles in the sea is believed to be rising.","explanation":"the number of (singular) / a number of (plural).","explanation_ar":"the number / a number."}],"theme_ar":"التحديات العالمية","essential_question_ar":"كيف يمكن للناس أن يتعاونوا لحل أكبر مشكلات العالم؟","can_do":"I can report information formally with the impersonal passive and passive infinitives, use collocations about global issues, and make verbs agree with tricky subjects.","can_do_ar":"أستطيع أن أنقل المعلومات بأسلوب رسمي بالمبني للمجهول غير الشخصي والمصدر المبني للمجهول، وأستخدم متلازمات القضايا العالمية، وأجعل الفعل يتفق مع الفاعل في الحالات الصعبة."});
